window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b091-902a719b99f7c696.json"]={sha256:"902a719b99f7c6960d3fdc2e6d3802097e30623166c4a7adcf0af99079dd72f6",value:{"id":"b091","title":"高層建築消防分區設計","titleEn":"Fire compartmentation in high-rise buildings","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從防火區劃的目的與火載量出發，比較灑水系統與區劃的分工，計算標準火災溫度與時間等效、防火門縫隙的漏煙、樓板邊緣縫隙的等效開口，再處理施工與裝修期間的區劃完整性、耐火試驗、樓梯加壓驗收、區劃失效時的結構臨界溫度，最後談使用管理與交接，並以高雄城中城大樓、倫敦 Grenfell Tower 與費城 One Meridian Plaza 的教訓對照。","summaryEn":"Starting from the purpose of compartmentation and fire load, compare the roles of sprinklers and compartments, compute standard-fire temperatures and time equivalence, smoke leakage through fire-door gaps and the equivalent opening of slab-edge gaps, then cover compartment integrity during construction and fit-out, fire-resistance testing, stair-pressurisation acceptance and structural critical temperatures when compartments fail, and finally management in use and handover, compared with lessons from Kaohsiung's Cheng Chung Cheng Building, London's Grenfell Tower and Philadelphia's One Meridian Plaza.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-seismic-precast-fire","subcategoryTitle":"建築耐震、預鑄與防火","subcategoryTitleEn":"Building seismic, precast and fire safety","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-seismic-precast-fire","learningTags":["structures","st-seismic-precast-fire","fire"],"architectureFamily":"fire","architectureNodes":[["起火區劃與火載量","Compartment of origin and fire load"],["灑水與消防水源","Sprinklers and fire water supply"],["區劃牆、樓板與防火門","Compartment walls, floors and fire doors"],["貫穿部與帷幕牆層間填塞","Penetrations and perimeter fire barriers"],["樓梯加壓與避難路徑","Stair pressurisation and escape routes"],["結構防火與管理紀錄","Structural fire protection and management records"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[0,2],[2,3],[2,4],[0,5],[3,5]],"diagram":{"type":"fire","labels":["起火區劃與火載量","灑水與消防水源","區劃牆、樓板與防火門","貫穿部與帷幕牆層間填塞","樓梯加壓與避難路徑"],"labelsEn":["Compartment of origin and fire load","Sprinklers and fire water supply","Compartment walls, floors and fire doors","Penetrations and perimeter fire barriers","Stair pressurisation and escape routes"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：某 40 層辦公大樓標準層 1,500 m²、火載量 600 MJ/m²，每層一個區劃，火載量 Q = 1,500×600 = 900 GJ。以 Eurocode 簡化時間等效 t_e = 600×0.07×1.0 ≈ 42 min，樓板與區劃牆採 60 min 防火時效；ISO 834 在 60 min 時約 945°C。主要鋼梁使用率 μ₀ = 0.5，臨界溫度約 585°C，被覆厚度依此選定。防火門 3 mm 周邊縫在 25 Pa 壓差下漏煙約 272 m³/h，多 20 mm 門下縫則加倍。帷幕牆與樓板 100 mm 縫、周長 160 m，若未封填等於每層 16 m² 開口。樓梯加壓 50 Pa 時開門力約 91.5 N，80 Pa 時約 122.5 N。若灑水系統失效使火勢跨越兩層，同時燃燒的火載量變為 1,800 GJ，鋼梁若因後續加載使用率升到 0.7，臨界溫度降為約 526°C，原被覆厚度不再足夠。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際建築的設計。","textEn":"Design exercise: a 40-storey office tower has 1,500 m² typical floors and a fire load of 600 MJ/m², one compartment per floor, so Q = 1,500×600 = 900 GJ. Simplified Eurocode time equivalence gives t_e = 600×0.07×1.0 ≈ 42 min, so floors and compartment walls are rated 60 min; ISO 834 reaches about 945°C at 60 min. Principal steel beams at utilisation μ₀ = 0.5 have a critical temperature of about 585°C, which sets the coating thickness. A fire door with a 3 mm perimeter gap leaks about 272 m³/h at 25 Pa, doubled by an extra 20 mm undercut. A 100 mm curtain-wall gap around a 160 m perimeter, unsealed, equals a 16 m² opening per floor. Stair pressurisation at 50 Pa gives a door-opening force of about 91.5 N, and at 80 Pa about 122.5 N. If sprinkler failure lets the fire span two floors, the fire load burning at once becomes 1,800 GJ, and if later loads raise beam utilisation to 0.7, the critical temperature falls to about 526°C and the original coating is no longer sufficient. Values are teaching assumptions, not the design of any real building.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b091-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「防火區劃的目的、面積與火載量」與「火災成長、灑水系統與區劃的分工」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Purpose, area and fire load of compartments\" and \"Fire growth, sprinklers and the division of labour with compartments\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b091-v13-01","title":"防火區劃的目的、面積與火載量：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Purpose, area and fire load of compartments: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「防火區劃面積」如何影響高層建築消防分區設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Compartment floor area” governs force, deformation or durability in “Fire compartmentation in high-rise buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"防火區劃把建築切成許多以耐火牆、樓板與防火門窗圍成的小盒子，讓火災與煙在一定時間內被限制在起火的盒子裡，爭取避難與消防搶救時間，並限制同時燃燒的面積，保護結構。水平區劃限制每層的燃燒面積，垂直區劃則以樓板、樓梯間與管道間阻止火煙向上蔓延。台灣建築技術規則以每 1,500 m² 為防火構造建築物的區劃原則，設有自動滅火設備時可減計面積；十一層以上樓層則依內裝材料以更小的面積區劃，反映高層救援困難。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「防火區劃面積」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compartmentation divides a building into boxes enclosed by fire-resisting walls, floors and fire doors and windows, so that fire and smoke stay in the box of origin for a defined time, buying time for evacuation and firefighting and limiting the area burning at once to protect the structure. Horizontal compartments limit the burning area on each floor, while vertical compartmentation uses floors, stair enclosures and shafts to stop upward spread. Taiwan's Building Technical Regulations take 1,500 m² as the basic compartment for fire-resistive buildings, allowing reduced counting where automatic suppression is installed, and require smaller compartments above the 10th floor depending on interior finishes, reflecting the difficulty of high-rise rescue. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Compartment floor area” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：火載量 Q = A·q。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Fire load Q = A·q.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要設了灑水系統，防火區劃就可有可無。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"With sprinklers installed, compartmentation is optional.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「防火區劃面積」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Compartment floor area”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-01-k1","title":"防火區劃的目的、面積與火載量","titleEn":"Purpose, area and fire load of compartments","text":"防火區劃把建築切成許多以耐火牆、樓板與防火門窗圍成的小盒子，讓火災與煙在一定時間內被限制在起火的盒子裡，爭取避難與消防搶救時間，並限制同時燃燒的面積，保護結構。水平區劃限制每層的燃燒面積，垂直區劃則以樓板、樓梯間與管道間阻止火煙向上蔓延。","textEn":"Compartmentation divides a building into boxes enclosed by fire-resisting walls, floors and fire doors and windows, so that fire and smoke stay in the box of origin for a defined time, buying time for evacuation and firefighting and limiting the area burning at once to protect the structure. Horizontal compartments limit the burning area on each floor, while vertical compartmentation uses floors, stair enclosures and shafts to stop upward spread.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要設了灑水系統，防火區劃就可有可無。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: With sprinklers installed, compartmentation is optional. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「防火區劃的目的、面積與火載量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Purpose, area and fire load of compartments\" is correct?","options":["只要設了灑水系統，防火區劃就可有可無。","防火區劃把建築切成許多以耐火牆、樓板與防火門窗圍成的小盒子，讓火災與煙在一定時間內被限制在起火的盒子裡，爭取避難與消防搶救時間，並限制同時燃燒的面積，保護結構。","防火區劃只是延緩火勢，真正滅火只能靠消防隊，所以區劃不必太嚴格。"],"optionsEn":["With sprinklers installed, compartmentation is optional.","Compartmentation divides a building into boxes enclosed by fire-resisting walls, floors and fire doors and windows, so that fire and smoke stay in the box of origin for a defined time, buying time for evacuation and firefighting and limiting the area burning at once to protect the structure.","Compartments only delay a fire and only firefighters extinguish it, so compartmentation need not be rigorous."],"answer":1,"explanation":"防火區劃把建築切成許多以耐火牆、樓板與防火門窗圍成的小盒子，讓火災與煙在一定時間內被限制在起火的盒子裡，爭取避難與消防搶救時間，並限制同時燃燒的面積，保護結構。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compartmentation divides a building into boxes enclosed by fire-resisting walls, floors and fire doors and windows, so that fire and smoke stay in the box of origin for a defined time, buying time for evacuation and firefighting and limiting the area burning at once to protect the structure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b091-v13-02","title":"防火區劃的目的、面積與火載量：定量估算","titleEn":"Purpose, area and fire load of compartments: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「防火區劃面積」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Compartment floor area” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：火載量 Q = A·q。區劃面積 1,500 m²、辦公室火載量密度 q = 600 MJ/m²：Q = 1,500×600 = 900,000 MJ = 900 GJ；若因設灑水系統使區劃面積加倍到 3,000 m²，可能同時燃燒的火載量也加倍到 1,800 GJ，前提是灑水系統確實有效。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Fire load Q = A·q. A 1,500 m² compartment with an office fire-load density q = 600 MJ/m² holds Q = 1,500×600 = 900,000 MJ = 900 GJ; if sprinklers allow the compartment to double to 3,000 m², the fire load that could burn at once also doubles to 1,800 GJ, on the assumption that the sprinklers actually work. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：設計階段以防火區劃圖標示每個區劃的範圍、面積、防火時效、防火門窗與貫穿部，並與建築、機電、帷幕牆圖套繪，確認區劃線在每一層都連續閉合；審查時核對灑水系統減計面積的條件是否成立。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: At design stage, a compartmentation plan shows each compartment's extent, area, rating, fire doors and windows and penetrations, overlaid with architectural, services and curtain-wall drawings to confirm that compartment lines close continuously on every floor; at review, check that the conditions for any sprinkler-based area allowance are met.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"火載量 Q = A·q。區劃面積 1,500 m²、辦公室火載量密度 q = 600 MJ/m²：Q = 1,500×600 = 900,000 MJ = 900 GJ；若因設灑水系統使區劃面積加倍到 3,000 m²，可能同時燃燒的火載量也加倍到 1,800 GJ，前提是灑水系統確實有效。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Fire load Q = A·q. A 1,500 m² compartment with an office fire-load density q = 600 MJ/m² holds Q = 1,500×600 = 900,000 MJ = 900 GJ; if sprinklers allow the compartment to double to 3,000 m², the fire load that could burn at once also doubles to 1,800 GJ, on the assumption that the sprinklers actually work. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「防火區劃的目的、面積與火載量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Purpose, area and fire load of compartments\", which statement holds?","options":["防火門只要是防火材料做的，開著也能擋火。","管線穿過防火牆後，用任何填縫材料補起來就可以。","火載量 Q = A·q。"],"optionsEn":["A fire door made of fire-resisting material still stops fire when left open.","After pipes pass through a fire wall, any filler material can seal the gap.","Fire load Q = A·q."],"answer":2,"explanation":"火載量 Q = A·q。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Fire load Q = A·q. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b091-v13-03","title":"防火區劃的目的、面積與火載量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Purpose, area and fire load of compartments: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「防火區劃面積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Compartment floor area” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"設計階段以防火區劃圖標示每個區劃的範圍、面積、防火時效、防火門窗與貫穿部，並與建築、機電、帷幕牆圖套繪，確認區劃線在每一層都連續閉合；審查時核對灑水系統減計面積的條件是否成立。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"At design stage, a compartmentation plan shows each compartment's extent, area, rating, fire doors and windows and penetrations, overlaid with architectural, services and curtain-wall drawings to confirm that compartment lines close continuously on every floor; at review, check that the conditions for any sprinkler-based area allowance are met. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：防火區劃圖應由建築師與消防、結構、機電專業共同簽認，並作為竣工交接文件的一部分；任何隔間變更都必須回到這張圖上檢討。","observationEn":"Site practice: The compartmentation plan should be signed jointly by the architect and the fire, structural and services disciplines and form part of the handover documents; any partition change must be reviewed against it.","failure":"注意干擾：若區劃線在平面上看似完整，但在天花板上方、架高地板下方或帷幕牆邊緣斷開，火煙會繞過區劃牆擴散，使整層甚至多層同時受害；以灑水系統放大區劃面積後，若灑水系統失效，燃燒面積就超過結構與救援的假設。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Compartment lines that look complete on plan but break above ceilings, below raised floors or at the curtain-wall edge let fire and smoke bypass the walls and involve whole floors or several floors at once; once sprinklers justify larger compartments, sprinkler failure leaves a burning area beyond what structure and rescue assumed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"設計階段以防火區劃圖標示每個區劃的範圍、面積、防火時效、防火門窗與貫穿部，並與建築、機電、帷幕牆圖套繪，確認區劃線在每一層都連續閉合；審查時核對灑水系統減計面積的條件是否成立。","textEn":"At design stage, a compartmentation plan shows each compartment's extent, area, rating, fire doors and windows and penetrations, overlaid with architectural, services and curtain-wall drawings to confirm that compartment lines close continuously on every floor; at review, check that the conditions for any sprinkler-based area allowance are met.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"防火區劃圖應由建築師與消防、結構、機電專業共同簽認，並作為竣工交接文件的一部分；任何隔間變更都必須回到這張圖上檢討。","textEn":"The compartmentation plan should be signed jointly by the architect and the fire, structural and services disciplines and form part of the handover documents; any partition change must be reviewed against it.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「防火區劃的目的、面積與火載量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Purpose, area and fire load of compartments\"?","options":["設計階段以防火區劃圖標示每個區劃的範圍、面積、防火時效、防火門窗與貫穿部，並與建築、機電、帷幕牆圖套繪，確認區劃線在每一層都連續閉合。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","樓梯加壓的壓力越大越安全。"],"optionsEn":["At design stage, a compartmentation plan shows each compartment's extent, area, rating, fire doors and windows and penetrations, overlaid with architectural, services and curtain-wall drawings to confirm that compartment lines close continuously on every floor.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The higher the stair pressurisation, the safer."],"answer":0,"explanation":"設計階段以防火區劃圖標示每個區劃的範圍、面積、防火時效、防火門窗與貫穿部，並與建築、機電、帷幕牆圖套繪，確認區劃線在每一層都連續閉合；審查時核對灑水系統減計面積的條件是否成立。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"At design stage, a compartmentation plan shows each compartment's extent, area, rating, fire doors and windows and penetrations, overlaid with architectural, services and curtain-wall drawings to confirm that compartment lines close continuously on every floor; at review, check that the conditions for any sprinkler-based area allowance are met. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b091-v13-04","title":"防火區劃的目的、面積與火載量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Purpose, area and fire load of compartments: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「防火區劃面積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Compartment floor area” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若區劃線在平面上看似完整，但在天花板上方、架高地板下方或帷幕牆邊緣斷開，火煙會繞過區劃牆擴散，使整層甚至多層同時受害；以灑水系統放大區劃面積後，若灑水系統失效，燃燒面積就超過結構與救援的假設。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Compartment lines that look complete on plan but break above ceilings, below raised floors or at the curtain-wall edge let fire and smoke bypass the walls and involve whole floors or several floors at once; once sprinklers justify larger compartments, sprinkler failure leaves a burning area beyond what structure and rescue assumed. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：台灣建築技術規則以每 1,500 m² 為防火構造建築物的區劃原則，設有自動滅火設備時可減計面積；十一層以上樓層則依內裝材料以更小的面積區劃，反映高層救援困難。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Taiwan's Building Technical Regulations take 1,500 m² as the basic compartment for fire-resistive buildings, allowing reduced counting where automatic suppression is installed, and require smaller compartments above the 10th floor depending on interior finishes, reflecting the difficulty of high-rise rescue.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要設了灑水系統，防火區劃就可有可無。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"With sprinklers installed, compartmentation is optional.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若區劃線在平面上看似完整，但在天花板上方、架高地板下方或帷幕牆邊緣斷開，火煙會繞過區劃牆擴散，使整層甚至多層同時受害；以灑水系統放大區劃面積後，若灑水系統失效，燃燒面積就超過結構與救援的假設。","textEn":"Compartment lines that look complete on plan but break above ceilings, below raised floors or at the curtain-wall edge let fire and smoke bypass the walls and involve whole floors or several floors at once; once sprinklers justify larger compartments, sprinkler failure leaves a burning area beyond what structure and rescue assumed.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「防火區劃的目的、面積與火載量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Purpose, area and fire load of compartments\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若區劃線在平面上看似完整，但在天花板上方、架高地板下方或帷幕牆邊緣斷開，火煙會繞過區劃牆擴散，使整層甚至多層同時受害。","防火區劃只是延緩火勢，真正滅火只能靠消防隊，所以區劃不必太嚴格。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Compartment lines that look complete on plan but break above ceilings, below raised floors or at the curtain-wall edge let fire and smoke bypass the walls and involve whole floors or several floors at once.","Compartments only delay a fire and only firefighters extinguish it, so compartmentation need not be rigorous."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若區劃線在平面上看似完整，但在天花板上方、架高地板下方或帷幕牆邊緣斷開，火煙會繞過區劃牆擴散，使整層甚至多層同時受害；以灑水系統放大區劃面積後，若灑水系統失效，燃燒面積就超過結構與救援的假設。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Compartment lines that look complete on plan but break above ceilings, below raised floors or at the curtain-wall edge let fire and smoke bypass the walls and involve whole floors or several floors at once; once sprinklers justify larger compartments, sprinkler failure leaves a burning area beyond what structure and rescue assumed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b091-v13-05","title":"火災成長、灑水系統與區劃的分工：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Fire growth, sprinklers and the division of labour with compartments: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「灑水頭與火災成長」如何影響高層建築消防分區設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sprinkler heads and fire growth” governs force, deformation or durability in “Fire compartmentation in high-rise buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"室內火災初期以近似時間平方成長，若在閃燃前被灑水系統控制，火勢就不會擴大到整個區劃；區劃則是灑水失效或火勢超出設計時的第二道防線。兩者缺一，風險就大增。1991 年費城 38 層的 One Meridian Plaza 從 22 樓起火，未設灑水的樓層接連燃燒，共燒毀 8 層、歷時超過 19 小時並造成 3 名消防員殉職；火勢直到第一個設有自動灑水的 30 樓才被 10 個灑水頭擋住。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「灑水頭與火災成長」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Early compartment fires grow roughly with the square of time; if sprinklers control the fire before flashover, it never spreads across the compartment, and compartmentation is the second line of defence if sprinklers fail or the fire exceeds their design. Lose either and risk rises sharply. In 1991 the 38-storey One Meridian Plaza in Philadelphia caught fire on the 22nd floor; unsprinklered floors burned one after another, eight floors were destroyed over more than 19 hours and three firefighters died, and the fire was stopped only on the 30th floor, the first with automatic sprinklers, where ten heads held it back. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Sprinkler heads and fire growth” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：t² 火災 Q = α·t²，快速成長 α = 0.0469 kW/s²：熱釋放率達 1 MW 需 t = √(1,000/0.0469) ≈ 146 s，達 5 MW 需 √(5,000/0.0469) ≈ 327 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A t² fire Q = α·t² with fast growth α = 0.0469 kW/s² reaches 1 MW at t = √(1,000/0.0469) ≈ 146 s and 5 MW at √(5,000/0.0469) ≈ 327 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「防火區劃只是延緩火勢，真正滅火只能靠消防隊，所以區劃不必太嚴格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Compartments only delay a fire and only firefighters extinguish it, so compartmentation need not be rigorous.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「灑水頭與火災成長」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Sprinkler heads and fire growth”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-05-k1","title":"火災成長、灑水系統與區劃的分工","titleEn":"Fire growth, sprinklers and the division of labour with compartments","text":"室內火災初期以近似時間平方成長，若在閃燃前被灑水系統控制，火勢就不會擴大到整個區劃；區劃則是灑水失效或火勢超出設計時的第二道防線。兩者缺一，風險就大增。","textEn":"Early compartment fires grow roughly with the square of time; if sprinklers control the fire before flashover, it never spreads across the compartment, and compartmentation is the second line of defence if sprinklers fail or the fire exceeds their design. Lose either and risk rises sharply.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：防火區劃只是延緩火勢，真正滅火只能靠消防隊，所以區劃不必太嚴格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Compartments only delay a fire and only firefighters extinguish it, so compartmentation need not be rigorous. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「火災成長、灑水系統與區劃的分工」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fire growth, sprinklers and the division of labour with compartments\" is correct?","options":["防火區劃只是延緩火勢，真正滅火只能靠消防隊，所以區劃不必太嚴格。","標示一小時防火時效的牆，在任何火災中都一定能撐一小時。","室內火災初期以近似時間平方成長，若在閃燃前被灑水系統控制，火勢就不會擴大到整個區劃；區劃則是灑水失效或火勢超出設計時的第二道防線。"],"optionsEn":["Compartments only delay a fire and only firefighters extinguish it, so compartmentation need not be rigorous.","A wall rated for one hour will always last one hour in any fire.","Early compartment fires grow roughly with the square of time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"室內火災初期以近似時間平方成長，若在閃燃前被灑水系統控制，火勢就不會擴大到整個區劃；區劃則是灑水失效或火勢超出設計時的第二道防線。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Early compartment fires grow roughly with the square of time; if sprinklers control the fire before flashover, it never spreads across the compartment, and compartmentation is the second line of defence if sprinklers fail or the fire exceeds their design. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b091-v13-06","title":"火災成長、灑水系統與區劃的分工：定量估算","titleEn":"Fire growth, sprinklers and the division of labour with compartments: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「灑水頭與火災成長」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sprinkler heads and fire growth” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：t² 火災 Q = α·t²，快速成長 α = 0.0469 kW/s²：熱釋放率達 1 MW 需 t = √(1,000/0.0469) ≈ 146 s，達 5 MW 需 √(5,000/0.0469) ≈ 327 s。灑水頭若在約 1 MW 前動作，火勢可被控制；延遲到 5 MW 以上，房間可能已接近閃燃。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A t² fire Q = α·t² with fast growth α = 0.0469 kW/s² reaches 1 MW at t = √(1,000/0.0469) ≈ 146 s and 5 MW at √(5,000/0.0469) ≈ 327 s. Sprinklers operating before about 1 MW can control the fire; delayed beyond 5 MW, the room may be near flashover. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以火災模擬或手算檢查灑水頭在設計火災下的動作時間，確認水源、消防泵、管徑與壓力能供應設計區域；竣工時做灑水系統的流量與壓力試驗，並核對每一層都設有灑水頭，沒有因裝修而被遮蔽或漏設的區域。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check sprinkler operating time under the design fire by fire modelling or hand calculation, and confirm that water supply, fire pumps, pipe sizes and pressure serve the design area; at completion run flow and pressure tests and verify sprinkler coverage on every floor, with no areas obstructed by fit-out or left unprotected.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"t² 火災 Q = α·t²，快速成長 α = 0.0469 kW/s²：熱釋放率達 1 MW 需 t = √(1,000/0.0469) ≈ 146 s，達 5 MW 需 √(5,000/0.0469) ≈ 327 s。灑水頭若在約 1 MW 前動作，火勢可被控制；延遲到 5 MW 以上，房間可能已接近閃燃。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A t² fire Q = α·t² with fast growth α = 0.0469 kW/s² reaches 1 MW at t = √(1,000/0.0469) ≈ 146 s and 5 MW at √(5,000/0.0469) ≈ 327 s. Sprinklers operating before about 1 MW can control the fire; delayed beyond 5 MW, the room may be near flashover. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「火災成長、灑水系統與區劃的分工」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fire growth, sprinklers and the division of labour with compartments\", which statement holds?","options":["t² 火災 Q = α·t²，快速成長 α = 0.0469 kW/s²：熱釋放率達 1 MW 需 t = √(1,000/0.0469) ≈ 146 s，達 5 MW 需 √(5,000/0.0469) ≈ 327 s。","樓板本身有防火時效，就代表上下樓層已經完全區劃。","只要材料本身不燃，組成的牆或門就自動具有防火時效。"],"optionsEn":["A t² fire Q = α·t² with fast growth α = 0.0469 kW/s² reaches 1 MW at t = √(1,000/0.0469) ≈ 146 s and 5 MW at √(5,000/0.0469) ≈ 327 s.","If the floor slab is fire-rated, the floors above and below are fully compartmented.","If the materials are non-combustible, the wall or door they form automatically has a fire rating."],"answer":0,"explanation":"t² 火災 Q = α·t²，快速成長 α = 0.0469 kW/s²：熱釋放率達 1 MW 需 t = √(1,000/0.0469) ≈ 146 s，達 5 MW 需 √(5,000/0.0469) ≈ 327 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A t² fire Q = α·t² with fast growth α = 0.0469 kW/s² reaches 1 MW at t = √(1,000/0.0469) ≈ 146 s and 5 MW at √(5,000/0.0469) ≈ 327 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b091-v13-07","title":"火災成長、灑水系統與區劃的分工：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fire growth, sprinklers and the division of labour with compartments: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「灑水頭與火災成長」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sprinkler heads and fire growth” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以火災模擬或手算檢查灑水頭在設計火災下的動作時間，確認水源、消防泵、管徑與壓力能供應設計區域；竣工時做灑水系統的流量與壓力試驗，並核對每一層都設有灑水頭，沒有因裝修而被遮蔽或漏設的區域。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check sprinkler operating time under the design fire by fire modelling or hand calculation, and confirm that water supply, fire pumps, pipe sizes and pressure serve the design area; at completion run flow and pressure tests and verify sprinkler coverage on every floor, with no areas obstructed by fit-out or left unprotected. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：業主與管理單位應把灑水系統、消防泵、立管減壓閥與緊急電源列為同一套維護與測試計畫，任何停水或停用都要事前通報並採取補償措施，例如加強巡查與臨時滅火設備。","observationEn":"Site practice: Owners and managers should treat sprinklers, fire pumps, standpipe pressure-reducing valves and emergency power as one maintenance and testing programme, notifying any shutdown in advance and adopting compensating measures such as extra patrols and temporary extinguishing equipment.","failure":"注意干擾：One Meridian Plaza 中消防立管的減壓閥設定不當，出水壓力不足，加上電力中斷，消防員無法有效滅火，火勢依靠窗戶與樓板逐層向上；灑水系統水源中斷時，世界貿易中心 7 號大樓的下層火災也同樣失控，顯示區劃必須獨立承受長時間火災。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: At One Meridian Plaza, misadjusted pressure-reducing valves on the standpipes delivered too little pressure and power was lost, so firefighters could not fight the fire effectively while it climbed floor by floor; when the sprinkler water supply was lost at World Trade Center 7, lower-floor fires likewise burned uncontrolled, showing that compartments must withstand long fires on their own. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以火災模擬或手算檢查灑水頭在設計火災下的動作時間，確認水源、消防泵、管徑與壓力能供應設計區域；竣工時做灑水系統的流量與壓力試驗，並核對每一層都設有灑水頭，沒有因裝修而被遮蔽或漏設的區域。","textEn":"Check sprinkler operating time under the design fire by fire modelling or hand calculation, and confirm that water supply, fire pumps, pipe sizes and pressure serve the design area; at completion run flow and pressure tests and verify sprinkler coverage on every floor, with no areas obstructed by fit-out or left unprotected.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"業主與管理單位應把灑水系統、消防泵、立管減壓閥與緊急電源列為同一套維護與測試計畫，任何停水或停用都要事前通報並採取補償措施，例如加強巡查與臨時滅火設備。","textEn":"Owners and managers should treat sprinklers, fire pumps, standpipe pressure-reducing valves and emergency power as one maintenance and testing programme, notifying any shutdown in advance and adopting compensating measures such as extra patrols and temporary extinguishing equipment.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「火災成長、灑水系統與區劃的分工」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fire growth, sprinklers and the division of labour with compartments\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以火災模擬或手算檢查灑水頭在設計火災下的動作時間，確認水源、消防泵、管徑與壓力能供應設計區域。","鋼構只要有防火被覆，區劃失效也不會影響結構安全。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Check sprinkler operating time under the design fire by fire modelling or hand calculation, and confirm that water supply, fire pumps, pipe sizes and pressure serve the design area.","Steelwork with fireproofing is safe even if compartmentation fails."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以火災模擬或手算檢查灑水頭在設計火災下的動作時間，確認水源、消防泵、管徑與壓力能供應設計區域；竣工時做灑水系統的流量與壓力試驗，並核對每一層都設有灑水頭，沒有因裝修而被遮蔽或漏設的區域。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check sprinkler operating time under the design fire by fire modelling or hand calculation, and confirm that water supply, fire pumps, pipe sizes and pressure serve the design area; at completion run flow and pressure tests and verify sprinkler coverage on every floor, with no areas obstructed by fit-out or left unprotected. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b091-v13-08","title":"火災成長、灑水系統與區劃的分工：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fire growth, sprinklers and the division of labour with compartments: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「灑水頭與火災成長」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sprinkler heads and fire growth” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"One Meridian Plaza 中消防立管的減壓閥設定不當，出水壓力不足，加上電力中斷，消防員無法有效滅火，火勢依靠窗戶與樓板逐層向上；灑水系統水源中斷時，世界貿易中心 7 號大樓的下層火災也同樣失控，顯示區劃必須獨立承受長時間火災。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"At One Meridian Plaza, misadjusted pressure-reducing valves on the standpipes delivered too little pressure and power was lost, so firefighters could not fight the fire effectively while it climbed floor by floor; when the sprinkler water supply was lost at World Trade Center 7, lower-floor fires likewise burned uncontrolled, showing that compartments must withstand long fires on their own. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：1991 年費城 38 層的 One Meridian Plaza 從 22 樓起火，未設灑水的樓層接連燃燒，共燒毀 8 層、歷時超過 19 小時並造成 3 名消防員殉職；火勢直到第一個設有自動灑水的 30 樓才被 10 個灑水頭擋住。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: In 1991 the 38-storey One Meridian Plaza in Philadelphia caught fire on the 22nd floor; unsprinklered floors burned one after another, eight floors were destroyed over more than 19 hours and three firefighters died, and the fire was stopped only on the 30th floor, the first with automatic sprinklers, where ten heads held it back.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「防火區劃只是延緩火勢，真正滅火只能靠消防隊，所以區劃不必太嚴格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Compartments only delay a fire and only firefighters extinguish it, so compartmentation need not be rigorous.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"One Meridian Plaza 中消防立管的減壓閥設定不當，出水壓力不足，加上電力中斷，消防員無法有效滅火，火勢依靠窗戶與樓板逐層向上；灑水系統水源中斷時，世界貿易中心 7 號大樓的下層火災也同樣失控，顯示區劃必須獨立承受長時間火災。","textEn":"At One Meridian Plaza, misadjusted pressure-reducing valves on the standpipes delivered too little pressure and power was lost, so firefighters could not fight the fire effectively while it climbed floor by floor; when the sprinkler water supply was lost at World Trade Center 7, lower-floor fires likewise burned uncontrolled, showing that compartments must withstand long fires on their own.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「火災成長、灑水系統與區劃的分工」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fire growth, sprinklers and the division of labour with compartments\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","標示一小時防火時效的牆，在任何火災中都一定能撐一小時。","One Meridian Plaza 中消防立管的減壓閥設定不當，出水壓力不足，加上電力中斷，消防員無法有效滅火，火勢依靠窗戶與樓板逐層向上。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A wall rated for one hour will always last one hour in any fire.","At One Meridian Plaza, misadjusted pressure-reducing valves on the standpipes delivered too little pressure and power was lost, so firefighters could not fight the fire effectively while it climbed floor by floor."],"answer":2,"explanation":"One Meridian Plaza 中消防立管的減壓閥設定不當，出水壓力不足，加上電力中斷，消防員無法有效滅火，火勢依靠窗戶與樓板逐層向上；灑水系統水源中斷時，世界貿易中心 7 號大樓的下層火災也同樣失控，顯示區劃必須獨立承受長時間火災。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"At One Meridian Plaza, misadjusted pressure-reducing valves on the standpipes delivered too little pressure and power was lost, so firefighters could not fight the fire effectively while it climbed floor by floor; when the sprinkler water supply was lost at World Trade Center 7, lower-floor fires likewise burned uncontrolled, showing that compartments must withstand long fires on their own. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b091-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「防火時效、標準火災與時間等效」與「防火門、自動關閉與漏煙」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Fire resistance, the standard fire and time equivalence\" and \"Fire doors, self-closing and smoke leakage\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b091-v13-09","title":"防火時效、標準火災與時間等效：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Fire resistance, the standard fire and time equivalence: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「區劃牆與樓板防火時效」如何影響高層建築消防分區設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fire rating of compartment walls and floors” governs force, deformation or durability in “Fire compartmentation in high-rise buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"區劃構件的防火時效，是在標準升溫曲線下維持承載、完整性（不讓火焰與熱氣穿過）與隔熱性（背火面溫升不超過限值）的時間。真實火災的強度取決於火載量與開口通風，與標準火災不同，因此工程上常用時間等效的觀念，把真實火災的嚴重度換算成標準火災的等效時間，與構件的防火時效比較。對高層建築而言，樓板同時是結構構件與垂直區劃，防火時效常比一般隔間牆高。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「區劃牆與樓板防火時效」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The fire resistance of a compartment element is the time it maintains load-bearing capacity, integrity against flames and hot gases and insulation, keeping the unexposed face temperature rise within limits, under the standard temperature–time curve. Real fire severity depends on fire load and ventilation and differs from the standard fire, so engineers use time equivalence to convert real severity into an equivalent standard-fire duration for comparison with the element's rating. In high-rise buildings the floor slab is both a structural member and the vertical compartment, so its rating is often higher than that of ordinary partitions. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Fire rating of compartment walls and floors” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：ISO 834 標準火災 T = 345·log₁₀(8t+1) + 20：t = 60 min 時 T = 345×log₁₀(481) + 20 ≈ 945°C，t = 120 min 時約 1,049°C。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The ISO 834 standard fire is T = 345·log₁₀(8t+1) + 20: at t = 60 min, T = 345×log₁₀(481) + 20 ≈ 945°C, and at 120 min about 1,049°C.","failure":"常見誤解：「標示一小時防火時效的牆，在任何火災中都一定能撐一小時。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A wall rated for one hour will always last one hour in any fire.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「區劃牆與樓板防火時效」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Fire rating of compartment walls and floors”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-09-k1","title":"防火時效、標準火災與時間等效","titleEn":"Fire resistance, the standard fire and time equivalence","text":"區劃構件的防火時效，是在標準升溫曲線下維持承載、完整性（不讓火焰與熱氣穿過）與隔熱性（背火面溫升不超過限值）的時間。真實火災的強度取決於火載量與開口通風，與標準火災不同，因此工程上常用時間等效的觀念，把真實火災的嚴重度換算成標準火災的等效時間，與構件的防火時效比較。","textEn":"The fire resistance of a compartment element is the time it maintains load-bearing capacity, integrity against flames and hot gases and insulation, keeping the unexposed face temperature rise within limits, under the standard temperature–time curve. Real fire severity depends on fire load and ventilation and differs from the standard fire, so engineers use time equivalence to convert real severity into an equivalent standard-fire duration for comparison with the element's rating.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：標示一小時防火時效的牆，在任何火災中都一定能撐一小時。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A wall rated for one hour will always last one hour in any fire. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「防火時效、標準火災與時間等效」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fire resistance, the standard fire and time equivalence\" is correct?","options":["區劃構件的防火時效，是在標準升溫曲線下維持承載、完整性（不讓火焰與熱氣穿過）與隔熱性（背火面溫升不超過限值）的時間。","標示一小時防火時效的牆，在任何火災中都一定能撐一小時。","防火門只要是防火材料做的，開著也能擋火。"],"optionsEn":["The fire resistance of a compartment element is the time it maintains load-bearing capacity, integrity against flames and hot gases and insulation, keeping the unexposed face temperature rise within limits, under the standard temperature–time curve.","A wall rated for one hour will always last one hour in any fire.","A fire door made of fire-resisting material still stops fire when left open."],"answer":0,"explanation":"區劃構件的防火時效，是在標準升溫曲線下維持承載、完整性（不讓火焰與熱氣穿過）與隔熱性（背火面溫升不超過限值）的時間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The fire resistance of a compartment element is the time it maintains load-bearing capacity, integrity against flames and hot gases and insulation, keeping the unexposed face temperature rise within limits, under the standard temperature–time curve. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b091-v13-10","title":"防火時效、標準火災與時間等效：定量估算","titleEn":"Fire resistance, the standard fire and time equivalence: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「區劃牆與樓板防火時效」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fire rating of compartment walls and floors” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：ISO 834 標準火災 T = 345·log₁₀(8t+1) + 20：t = 60 min 時 T = 345×log₁₀(481) + 20 ≈ 945°C，t = 120 min 時約 1,049°C。以 Eurocode 簡化時間等效 t_e = q·k_b·w_f，q = 600 MJ/m²、k_b = 0.07 min·m²/MJ、w_f = 1.0：t_e = 600×0.07×1.0 ≈ 42 min，小於 60 min 防火時效。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The ISO 834 standard fire is T = 345·log₁₀(8t+1) + 20: at t = 60 min, T = 345×log₁₀(481) + 20 ≈ 945°C, and at 120 min about 1,049°C. With the simplified Eurocode time equivalence t_e = q·k_b·w_f, q = 600 MJ/m², k_b = 0.07 min·m²/MJ and w_f = 1.0, t_e = 600×0.07×1.0 ≈ 42 min, below a 60-minute rating. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對每種區劃牆、樓板、防火門窗與貫穿系統都有經認可的耐火試驗或認證，試驗構造與現場構造（材料、厚度、固定方式、尺寸）一致；採性能設計時，火載量與通風假設須有調查依據並經審查。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Confirm that every compartment wall, floor, fire door and window and penetration system has an approved fire test or listing, and that the tested construction matches the site construction in materials, thickness, fixing and size; where performance-based design is used, fire-load and ventilation assumptions must be based on survey data and reviewed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"ISO 834 標準火災 T = 345·log₁₀(8t+1) + 20：t = 60 min 時 T = 345×log₁₀(481) + 20 ≈ 945°C，t = 120 min 時約 1,049°C。以 Eurocode 簡化時間等效 t_e = q·k_b·w_f，q = 600 MJ/m²、k_b = 0.07 min·m²/MJ、w_f = 1.0：t_e = 600×0.07×1.0 ≈ 42 min，小於 60 min 防火時效。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The ISO 834 standard fire is T = 345·log₁₀(8t+1) + 20: at t = 60 min, T = 345×log₁₀(481) + 20 ≈ 945°C, and at 120 min about 1,049°C. With the simplified Eurocode time equivalence t_e = q·k_b·w_f, q = 600 MJ/m², k_b = 0.07 min·m²/MJ and w_f = 1.0, t_e = 600×0.07×1.0 ≈ 42 min, below a 60-minute rating. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「防火時效、標準火災與時間等效」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fire resistance, the standard fire and time equivalence\", which statement holds?","options":["管線穿過防火牆後，用任何填縫材料補起來就可以。","ISO 834 標準火災 T = 345·log₁₀(8t+1) + 20：t = 60 min 時 T = 345×log₁₀(481) + 20 ≈ 945°C，t = 120 min 時約 1,049°C。","樓梯加壓的壓力越大越安全。"],"optionsEn":["After pipes pass through a fire wall, any filler material can seal the gap.","The ISO 834 standard fire is T = 345·log₁₀(8t+1) + 20: at t = 60 min, T = 345×log₁₀(481) + 20 ≈ 945°C, and at 120 min about 1,049°C.","The higher the stair pressurisation, the safer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"ISO 834 標準火災 T = 345·log₁₀(8t+1) + 20：t = 60 min 時 T = 345×log₁₀(481) + 20 ≈ 945°C，t = 120 min 時約 1,049°C。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The ISO 834 standard fire is T = 345·log₁₀(8t+1) + 20: at t = 60 min, T = 345×log₁₀(481) + 20 ≈ 945°C, and at 120 min about 1,049°C. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b091-v13-11","title":"防火時效、標準火災與時間等效：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fire resistance, the standard fire and time equivalence: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「區劃牆與樓板防火時效」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fire rating of compartment walls and floors” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對每種區劃牆、樓板、防火門窗與貫穿系統都有經認可的耐火試驗或認證，試驗構造與現場構造（材料、厚度、固定方式、尺寸）一致；採性能設計時，火載量與通風假設須有調查依據並經審查。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Confirm that every compartment wall, floor, fire door and window and penetration system has an approved fire test or listing, and that the tested construction matches the site construction in materials, thickness, fixing and size; where performance-based design is used, fire-load and ventilation assumptions must be based on survey data and reviewed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：防火構造的材料送審要附耐火試驗報告與構造詳圖，現場依詳圖施作並由監造逐區查驗；使用用途改變為高火載量時，須重新檢討防火時效。","observationEn":"Site practice: Submittals for fire-resisting construction must include fire test reports and construction details, with site work following the details and inspected area by area; any change to a high-fire-load use requires the ratings to be reassessed.","failure":"注意干擾：若現場以未經試驗的輕隔間或板材替代，或固定間距、板材層數與試驗不同，區劃牆在火災中提早失去完整性；倉儲或資料中心等高火載量用途若沿用辦公室的時間等效，真實火災會超過構件的防火時效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Substituting untested partitions or boards on site, or changing fixing spacing or board layers from the tested build-up, makes compartment walls lose integrity early in a fire; applying office time equivalence to high-fire-load uses such as storage or data centres lets real fires exceed element ratings. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對每種區劃牆、樓板、防火門窗與貫穿系統都有經認可的耐火試驗或認證，試驗構造與現場構造（材料、厚度、固定方式、尺寸）一致；採性能設計時，火載量與通風假設須有調查依據並經審查。","textEn":"Confirm that every compartment wall, floor, fire door and window and penetration system has an approved fire test or listing, and that the tested construction matches the site construction in materials, thickness, fixing and size; where performance-based design is used, fire-load and ventilation assumptions must be based on survey data and reviewed.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"防火構造的材料送審要附耐火試驗報告與構造詳圖，現場依詳圖施作並由監造逐區查驗；使用用途改變為高火載量時，須重新檢討防火時效。","textEn":"Submittals for fire-resisting construction must include fire test reports and construction details, with site work following the details and inspected area by area; any change to a high-fire-load use requires the ratings to be reassessed.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「防火時效、標準火災與時間等效」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fire resistance, the standard fire and time equivalence\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","老舊建築只要當年合法取得使用執照，就不需要再檢討防火區劃。","核對每種區劃牆、樓板、防火門窗與貫穿系統都有經認可的耐火試驗或認證，試驗構造與現場構造（材料、厚度、固定方式、尺寸）一致。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","An old building that was lawfully approved when built needs no further review of its compartmentation.","Confirm that every compartment wall, floor, fire door and window and penetration system has an approved fire test or listing, and that the tested construction matches the site construction in materials, thickness, fixing and size."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對每種區劃牆、樓板、防火門窗與貫穿系統都有經認可的耐火試驗或認證，試驗構造與現場構造（材料、厚度、固定方式、尺寸）一致；採性能設計時，火載量與通風假設須有調查依據並經審查。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Confirm that every compartment wall, floor, fire door and window and penetration system has an approved fire test or listing, and that the tested construction matches the site construction in materials, thickness, fixing and size; where performance-based design is used, fire-load and ventilation assumptions must be based on survey data and reviewed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b091-v13-12","title":"防火時效、標準火災與時間等效：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fire resistance, the standard fire and time equivalence: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「區劃牆與樓板防火時效」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fire rating of compartment walls and floors” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若現場以未經試驗的輕隔間或板材替代，或固定間距、板材層數與試驗不同，區劃牆在火災中提早失去完整性；倉儲或資料中心等高火載量用途若沿用辦公室的時間等效，真實火災會超過構件的防火時效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Substituting untested partitions or boards on site, or changing fixing spacing or board layers from the tested build-up, makes compartment walls lose integrity early in a fire; applying office time equivalence to high-fire-load uses such as storage or data centres lets real fires exceed element ratings. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：對高層建築而言，樓板同時是結構構件與垂直區劃，防火時效常比一般隔間牆高。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: In high-rise buildings the floor slab is both a structural member and the vertical compartment, so its rating is often higher than that of ordinary partitions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「標示一小時防火時效的牆，在任何火災中都一定能撐一小時。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A wall rated for one hour will always last one hour in any fire.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若現場以未經試驗的輕隔間或板材替代，或固定間距、板材層數與試驗不同，區劃牆在火災中提早失去完整性；倉儲或資料中心等高火載量用途若沿用辦公室的時間等效，真實火災會超過構件的防火時效。","textEn":"Substituting untested partitions or boards on site, or changing fixing spacing or board layers from the tested build-up, makes compartment walls lose integrity early in a fire; applying office time equivalence to high-fire-load uses such as storage or data centres lets real fires exceed element ratings.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「防火時效、標準火災與時間等效」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fire resistance, the standard fire and time equivalence\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若現場以未經試驗的輕隔間或板材替代，或固定間距、板材層數與試驗不同，區劃牆在火災中提早失去完整性。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","防火門只要是防火材料做的，開著也能擋火。"],"optionsEn":["Substituting untested partitions or boards on site, or changing fixing spacing or board layers from the tested build-up, makes compartment walls lose integrity early in a fire.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A fire door made of fire-resisting material still stops fire when left open."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若現場以未經試驗的輕隔間或板材替代，或固定間距、板材層數與試驗不同，區劃牆在火災中提早失去完整性；倉儲或資料中心等高火載量用途若沿用辦公室的時間等效，真實火災會超過構件的防火時效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Substituting untested partitions or boards on site, or changing fixing spacing or board layers from the tested build-up, makes compartment walls lose integrity early in a fire; applying office time equivalence to high-fire-load uses such as storage or data centres lets real fires exceed element ratings. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b091-v13-13","title":"防火門、自動關閉與漏煙：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Fire doors, self-closing and smoke leakage: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「防火門與門縫」如何影響高層建築消防分區設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fire doors and door gaps” governs force, deformation or durability in “Fire compartmentation in high-rise buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"防火門是區劃上最常被打開的缺口：門必須自動關閉並緊密閉合，門框與牆的接縫、門下縫與門扇周邊縫都會漏煙。高層建築的煙囪效應與加壓系統使門兩側存在壓力差，即使只有數公釐的縫隙，也能讓大量煙進入走廊或樓梯。Grenfell Tower 火災中，住戶單元的防火門未能自動關閉與密封，使煙從住戶進入梯廳；事前的防火缺失通知也已列出防火門問題。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「防火門與門縫」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Fire doors are the most frequently opened gaps in a compartment: they must self-close and latch tightly, and frame-to-wall joints, undercuts and leaf perimeters all leak smoke. Stack effect and pressurisation in tall buildings create pressure differences across doors, so even gaps of a few millimetres admit large amounts of smoke into corridors or stairs. In the Grenfell Tower fire, flat entrance fire doors failed to close and seal, letting smoke pass from flats into lobbies, and an earlier fire deficiency notice had already listed fire-door problems. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Fire doors and door gaps” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：孔口流量 Q = C·A·√(2ΔP/ρ)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Orifice flow Q = C·A·√(2ΔP/ρ).","failure":"常見誤解：「防火門只要是防火材料做的，開著也能擋火。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A fire door made of fire-resisting material still stops fire when left open.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「防火門與門縫」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Fire doors and door gaps”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-13-k1","title":"防火門、自動關閉與漏煙","titleEn":"Fire doors, self-closing and smoke leakage","text":"防火門是區劃上最常被打開的缺口：門必須自動關閉並緊密閉合，門框與牆的接縫、門下縫與門扇周邊縫都會漏煙。高層建築的煙囪效應與加壓系統使門兩側存在壓力差，即使只有數公釐的縫隙，也能讓大量煙進入走廊或樓梯。","textEn":"Fire doors are the most frequently opened gaps in a compartment: they must self-close and latch tightly, and frame-to-wall joints, undercuts and leaf perimeters all leak smoke. Stack effect and pressurisation in tall buildings create pressure differences across doors, so even gaps of a few millimetres admit large amounts of smoke into corridors or stairs.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：防火門只要是防火材料做的，開著也能擋火。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A fire door made of fire-resisting material still stops fire when left open. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「防火門、自動關閉與漏煙」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fire doors, self-closing and smoke leakage\" is correct?","options":["防火門只要是防火材料做的，開著也能擋火。","防火門是區劃上最常被打開的缺口：門必須自動關閉並緊密閉合，門框與牆的接縫、門下縫與門扇周邊縫都會漏煙。","樓板本身有防火時效，就代表上下樓層已經完全區劃。"],"optionsEn":["A fire door made of fire-resisting material still stops fire when left open.","Fire doors are the most frequently opened gaps in a compartment: they must self-close and latch tightly, and frame-to-wall joints, undercuts and leaf perimeters all leak smoke.","If the floor slab is fire-rated, the floors above and below are fully compartmented."],"answer":1,"explanation":"防火門是區劃上最常被打開的缺口：門必須自動關閉並緊密閉合，門框與牆的接縫、門下縫與門扇周邊縫都會漏煙。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Fire doors are the most frequently opened gaps in a compartment: they must self-close and latch tightly, and frame-to-wall joints, undercuts and leaf perimeters all leak smoke. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b091-v13-14","title":"防火門、自動關閉與漏煙：定量估算","titleEn":"Fire doors, self-closing and smoke leakage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「防火門與門縫」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fire doors and door gaps” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：孔口流量 Q = C·A·√(2ΔP/ρ)。2.1 m × 0.9 m 門扇周邊縫 3 mm，A = 0.003×(2×2.1 + 2×0.9) = 0.018 m²；ΔP = 25 Pa、ρ = 1.2 kg/m³、C = 0.65：v = √(2×25/1.2) ≈ 6.45 m/s，Q ≈ 0.65×0.018×6.45 ≈ 0.076 m³/s（約 272 m³/h）。門下縫再多 20 mm，面積加倍，漏煙量增為約 544 m³/h。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Orifice flow Q = C·A·√(2ΔP/ρ). A 2.1 m × 0.9 m door leaf with a 3 mm perimeter gap has A = 0.003×(2×2.1 + 2×0.9) = 0.018 m²; with ΔP = 25 Pa, ρ = 1.2 kg/m³ and C = 0.65, v = √(2×25/1.2) ≈ 6.45 m/s and Q ≈ 0.65×0.018×6.45 ≈ 0.076 m³/s, about 272 m³/h. A further 20 mm undercut doubles the area and leakage to about 544 m³/h. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：竣工時逐樘檢查防火門的認證標籤、門弓器自動關閉與閂鎖、門縫尺寸與防煙條，並抽樣做關閉時間測試；與消防受信總機連動的常開防火門，要實際觸發偵測器確認會關閉。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: At completion check every fire door's certification label, closer self-closing and latching, gap sizes and smoke seals, and test closing time on a sample; for hold-open doors linked to the fire alarm panel, trigger the detectors to confirm they close.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"孔口流量 Q = C·A·√(2ΔP/ρ)。2.1 m × 0.9 m 門扇周邊縫 3 mm，A = 0.003×(2×2.1 + 2×0.9) = 0.018 m²；ΔP = 25 Pa、ρ = 1.2 kg/m³、C = 0.65：v = √(2×25/1.2) ≈ 6.45 m/s，Q ≈ 0.65×0.018×6.45 ≈ 0.076 m³/s（約 272 m³/h）。門下縫再多 20 mm，面積加倍，漏煙量增為約 544 m³/h。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Orifice flow Q = C·A·√(2ΔP/ρ). A 2.1 m × 0.9 m door leaf with a 3 mm perimeter gap has A = 0.003×(2×2.1 + 2×0.9) = 0.018 m²; with ΔP = 25 Pa, ρ = 1.2 kg/m³ and C = 0.65, v = √(2×25/1.2) ≈ 6.45 m/s and Q ≈ 0.65×0.018×6.45 ≈ 0.076 m³/s, about 272 m³/h. A further 20 mm undercut doubles the area and leakage to about 544 m³/h. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「防火門、自動關閉與漏煙」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fire doors, self-closing and smoke leakage\", which statement holds?","options":["只要材料本身不燃，組成的牆或門就自動具有防火時效。","鋼構只要有防火被覆，區劃失效也不會影響結構安全。","孔口流量 Q = C·A·√(2ΔP/ρ)。"],"optionsEn":["If the materials are non-combustible, the wall or door they form automatically has a fire rating.","Steelwork with fireproofing is safe even if compartmentation fails.","Orifice flow Q = C·A·√(2ΔP/ρ)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"孔口流量 Q = C·A·√(2ΔP/ρ)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Orifice flow Q = C·A·√(2ΔP/ρ). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b091-v13-15","title":"防火門、自動關閉與漏煙：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fire doors, self-closing and smoke leakage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「防火門與門縫」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fire doors and door gaps” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"竣工時逐樘檢查防火門的認證標籤、門弓器自動關閉與閂鎖、門縫尺寸與防煙條，並抽樣做關閉時間測試；與消防受信總機連動的常開防火門，要實際觸發偵測器確認會關閉。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"At completion check every fire door's certification label, closer self-closing and latching, gap sizes and smoke seals, and test closing time on a sample; for hold-open doors linked to the fire alarm panel, trigger the detectors to confirm they close. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：管理規約應禁止撐開防火門，需要常開者必須改為與偵測器連動的自動關閉裝置；防火門的五金更換須使用經認證的配件，並列入定期檢查表。","observationEn":"Site practice: House rules should forbid propping fire doors open, with doors that must stay open fitted with detector-linked automatic release; door hardware replacements must use certified components and be included in periodic inspections.","failure":"注意干擾：防火門被楔子撐開、門弓器拆除或門扇變形無法閂鎖時，起火區的煙直接灌入走廊與樓梯，使逃生路徑在數分鐘內失去可用性；更換門鎖或加裝貓眼若破壞門扇構造，也會讓防火門失去認證性能。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fire doors wedged open, closers removed or leaves warped so they cannot latch let smoke pour straight into corridors and stairs, making escape routes unusable within minutes; replacing locks or adding viewers in a way that breaks the leaf construction also voids the door's certified performance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"竣工時逐樘檢查防火門的認證標籤、門弓器自動關閉與閂鎖、門縫尺寸與防煙條，並抽樣做關閉時間測試；與消防受信總機連動的常開防火門，要實際觸發偵測器確認會關閉。","textEn":"At completion check every fire door's certification label, closer self-closing and latching, gap sizes and smoke seals, and test closing time on a sample; for hold-open doors linked to the fire alarm panel, trigger the detectors to confirm they close.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"管理規約應禁止撐開防火門，需要常開者必須改為與偵測器連動的自動關閉裝置；防火門的五金更換須使用經認證的配件，並列入定期檢查表。","textEn":"House rules should forbid propping fire doors open, with doors that must stay open fitted with detector-linked automatic release; door hardware replacements must use certified components and be included in periodic inspections.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「防火門、自動關閉與漏煙」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fire doors, self-closing and smoke leakage\"?","options":["竣工時逐樘檢查防火門的認證標籤、門弓器自動關閉與閂鎖、門縫尺寸與防煙條，並抽樣做關閉時間測試；與消防受信總機連動的常開防火門，要實際觸發偵測器確認會關閉。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要設了灑水系統，防火區劃就可有可無。"],"optionsEn":["At completion check every fire door's certification label, closer self-closing and latching, gap sizes and smoke seals, and test closing time on a sample.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","With sprinklers installed, compartmentation is optional."],"answer":0,"explanation":"竣工時逐樘檢查防火門的認證標籤、門弓器自動關閉與閂鎖、門縫尺寸與防煙條，並抽樣做關閉時間測試；與消防受信總機連動的常開防火門，要實際觸發偵測器確認會關閉。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"At completion check every fire door's certification label, closer self-closing and latching, gap sizes and smoke seals, and test closing time on a sample; for hold-open doors linked to the fire alarm panel, trigger the detectors to confirm they close. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b091-v13-16","title":"防火門、自動關閉與漏煙：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fire doors, self-closing and smoke leakage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「防火門與門縫」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fire doors and door gaps” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"防火門被楔子撐開、門弓器拆除或門扇變形無法閂鎖時，起火區的煙直接灌入走廊與樓梯，使逃生路徑在數分鐘內失去可用性；更換門鎖或加裝貓眼若破壞門扇構造，也會讓防火門失去認證性能。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fire doors wedged open, closers removed or leaves warped so they cannot latch let smoke pour straight into corridors and stairs, making escape routes unusable within minutes; replacing locks or adding viewers in a way that breaks the leaf construction also voids the door's certified performance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：Grenfell Tower 火災中，住戶單元的防火門未能自動關閉與密封，使煙從住戶進入梯廳；事前的防火缺失通知也已列出防火門問題。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: In the Grenfell Tower fire, flat entrance fire doors failed to close and seal, letting smoke pass from flats into lobbies, and an earlier fire deficiency notice had already listed fire-door problems.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「防火門只要是防火材料做的，開著也能擋火。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A fire door made of fire-resisting material still stops fire when left open.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"防火門被楔子撐開、門弓器拆除或門扇變形無法閂鎖時，起火區的煙直接灌入走廊與樓梯，使逃生路徑在數分鐘內失去可用性；更換門鎖或加裝貓眼若破壞門扇構造，也會讓防火門失去認證性能。","textEn":"Fire doors wedged open, closers removed or leaves warped so they cannot latch let smoke pour straight into corridors and stairs, making escape routes unusable within minutes; replacing locks or adding viewers in a way that breaks the leaf construction also voids the door's certified performance.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「防火門、自動關閉與漏煙」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fire doors, self-closing and smoke leakage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","防火門被楔子撐開、門弓器拆除或門扇變形無法閂鎖時，起火區的煙直接灌入走廊與樓梯，使逃生路徑在數分鐘內失去可用性。","樓板本身有防火時效，就代表上下樓層已經完全區劃。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Fire doors wedged open, closers removed or leaves warped so they cannot latch let smoke pour straight into corridors and stairs, making escape routes unusable within minutes.","If the floor slab is fire-rated, the floors above and below are fully compartmented."],"answer":1,"explanation":"防火門被楔子撐開、門弓器拆除或門扇變形無法閂鎖時，起火區的煙直接灌入走廊與樓梯，使逃生路徑在數分鐘內失去可用性；更換門鎖或加裝貓眼若破壞門扇構造，也會讓防火門失去認證性能。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fire doors wedged open, closers removed or leaves warped so they cannot latch let smoke pour straight into corridors and stairs, making escape routes unusable within minutes; replacing locks or adding viewers in a way that breaks the leaf construction also voids the door's certified performance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b091-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「樓板邊緣、帷幕牆與外牆的垂直蔓延」與「施工與裝修期間的區劃完整性」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Slab edges, curtain walls and vertical spread on the façade\" and \"Compartment integrity during construction and fit-out\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b091-v13-17","title":"樓板邊緣、帷幕牆與外牆的垂直蔓延：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Slab edges, curtain walls and vertical spread on the façade: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「帷幕牆層間防火」如何影響高層建築消防分區設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Curtain-wall perimeter fire barrier” governs force, deformation or durability in “Fire compartmentation in high-rise buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"高層建築的垂直區劃常在樓板邊緣斷開：帷幕牆與樓板之間留有施工縫，若沒有以經試驗的層間防火填塞封閉，火煙會沿縫隙直接竄上樓。外牆本身也可能成為火的通道，Grenfell Tower 在 2015 至 2016 年改裝時加上鋁複合板與可燃保溫材，火災時火焰沿外牆空腔向上，繞過內部的區劃，約 30 分鐘內抵達屋頂，公開調查第一階段報告指出外牆是火勢快速蔓延的主因。設計上要同時處理樓板邊緣填塞、窗間牆高度與外牆材料的燃燒性。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「帷幕牆層間防火」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Vertical compartmentation in tall buildings often breaks at the slab edge: a construction gap between curtain wall and floor, if not closed with a tested perimeter fire barrier, lets fire and smoke rise straight up. The façade itself can also become a fire path; Grenfell Tower was overclad in 2015 to 2016 with aluminium composite panels and combustible insulation, and in the fire flames travelled up the external cavity, bypassing internal compartments and reaching the roof within about 30 minutes, with the inquiry's Phase 1 report identifying the exterior as the principal reason for the rapid spread. Design must address slab-edge firestopping, spandrel height and façade combustibility together. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Curtain-wall perimeter fire barrier” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：樓板外周長 160 m、帷幕牆與樓板之間的縫寬 100 mm，若完全未封填，每層等效開口 A = 0.10×160 = 16 m²，相當於樓板上一個 4 m × 4 m 的洞；即使只有 10% 長度漏封，也有約 1.6 m² 的垂直通道。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With a 160 m slab perimeter and a 100 mm gap between curtain wall and slab, an unsealed gap is an equivalent opening of A = 0.10×160 = 16 m² per floor, like a 4 m × 4 m hole in the slab; even 10% of the length left unsealed is a vertical path of about 1.6 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「樓板本身有防火時效，就代表上下樓層已經完全區劃。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the floor slab is fire-rated, the floors above and below are fully compartmented.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「帷幕牆層間防火」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Curtain-wall perimeter fire barrier”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-17-k1","title":"樓板邊緣、帷幕牆與外牆的垂直蔓延","titleEn":"Slab edges, curtain walls and vertical spread on the façade","text":"高層建築的垂直區劃常在樓板邊緣斷開：帷幕牆與樓板之間留有施工縫，若沒有以經試驗的層間防火填塞封閉，火煙會沿縫隙直接竄上樓。外牆本身也可能成為火的通道，Grenfell Tower 在 2015 至 2016 年改裝時加上鋁複合板與可燃保溫材，火災時火焰沿外牆空腔向上，繞過內部的區劃，約 30 分鐘內抵達屋頂，公開調查第一階段報告指出外牆是火勢快速蔓延的主因。","textEn":"Vertical compartmentation in tall buildings often breaks at the slab edge: a construction gap between curtain wall and floor, if not closed with a tested perimeter fire barrier, lets fire and smoke rise straight up. The façade itself can also become a fire path; Grenfell Tower was overclad in 2015 to 2016 with aluminium composite panels and combustible insulation, and in the fire flames travelled up the external cavity, bypassing internal compartments and reaching the roof within about 30 minutes, with the inquiry's Phase 1 report identifying the exterior as the principal reason for the rapid spread.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：樓板本身有防火時效，就代表上下樓層已經完全區劃。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the floor slab is fire-rated, the floors above and below are fully compartmented. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「樓板邊緣、帷幕牆與外牆的垂直蔓延」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Slab edges, curtain walls and vertical spread on the façade\" is correct?","options":["樓板本身有防火時效，就代表上下樓層已經完全區劃。","管線穿過防火牆後，用任何填縫材料補起來就可以。","高層建築的垂直區劃常在樓板邊緣斷開：帷幕牆與樓板之間留有施工縫，若沒有以經試驗的層間防火填塞封閉，火煙會沿縫隙直接竄上樓。"],"optionsEn":["If the floor slab is fire-rated, the floors above and below are fully compartmented.","After pipes pass through a fire wall, any filler material can seal the gap.","Vertical compartmentation in tall buildings often breaks at the slab edge: a construction gap between curtain wall and floor, if not closed with a tested perimeter fire barrier, lets fire and smoke rise straight up."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高層建築的垂直區劃常在樓板邊緣斷開：帷幕牆與樓板之間留有施工縫，若沒有以經試驗的層間防火填塞封閉，火煙會沿縫隙直接竄上樓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Vertical compartmentation in tall buildings often breaks at the slab edge: a construction gap between curtain wall and floor, if not closed with a tested perimeter fire barrier, lets fire and smoke rise straight up. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b091-v13-18","title":"樓板邊緣、帷幕牆與外牆的垂直蔓延：定量估算","titleEn":"Slab edges, curtain walls and vertical spread on the façade: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「帷幕牆層間防火」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Curtain-wall perimeter fire barrier” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：樓板外周長 160 m、帷幕牆與樓板之間的縫寬 100 mm，若完全未封填，每層等效開口 A = 0.10×160 = 16 m²，相當於樓板上一個 4 m × 4 m 的洞；即使只有 10% 長度漏封，也有約 1.6 m² 的垂直通道。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With a 160 m slab perimeter and a 100 mm gap between curtain wall and slab, an unsealed gap is an equivalent opening of A = 0.10×160 = 16 m² per floor, like a 4 m × 4 m hole in the slab; even 10% of the length left unsealed is a vertical path of about 1.6 m². Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：層間防火填塞必須採用與帷幕牆型式一致的試驗系統，現場檢查礦棉密度、壓縮率、支撐角鐵與表面防煙密封，並逐層拍照；外牆材料須有燃燒性能證明，帷幕牆設計審查時把窗間牆與層間填塞一併檢核。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Perimeter fire barriers must be a tested system matching the curtain-wall type, with mineral-wool density, compression, support angles and surface smoke seal inspected and photographed floor by floor; façade materials need combustibility evidence, and curtain-wall design review checks spandrels and perimeter barriers together.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"樓板外周長 160 m、帷幕牆與樓板之間的縫寬 100 mm，若完全未封填，每層等效開口 A = 0.10×160 = 16 m²，相當於樓板上一個 4 m × 4 m 的洞；即使只有 10% 長度漏封，也有約 1.6 m² 的垂直通道。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"With a 160 m slab perimeter and a 100 mm gap between curtain wall and slab, an unsealed gap is an equivalent opening of A = 0.10×160 = 16 m² per floor, like a 4 m × 4 m hole in the slab; even 10% of the length left unsealed is a vertical path of about 1.6 m². Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「樓板邊緣、帷幕牆與外牆的垂直蔓延」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Slab edges, curtain walls and vertical spread on the façade\", which statement holds?","options":["樓板外周長 160 m、帷幕牆與樓板之間的縫寬 100 mm，若完全未封填，每層等效開口 A = 0.10×160 = 16 m²，相當於樓板上一個 4 m × 4 m 的洞。","樓梯加壓的壓力越大越安全。","老舊建築只要當年合法取得使用執照，就不需要再檢討防火區劃。"],"optionsEn":["With a 160 m slab perimeter and a 100 mm gap between curtain wall and slab, an unsealed gap is an equivalent opening of A = 0.10×160 = 16 m² per floor, like a 4 m × 4 m hole in the slab.","The higher the stair pressurisation, the safer.","An old building that was lawfully approved when built needs no further review of its compartmentation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"樓板外周長 160 m、帷幕牆與樓板之間的縫寬 100 mm，若完全未封填，每層等效開口 A = 0.10×160 = 16 m²，相當於樓板上一個 4 m × 4 m 的洞；即使只有 10% 長度漏封，也有約 1.6 m² 的垂直通道。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With a 160 m slab perimeter and a 100 mm gap between curtain wall and slab, an unsealed gap is an equivalent opening of A = 0.10×160 = 16 m² per floor, like a 4 m × 4 m hole in the slab; even 10% of the length left unsealed is a vertical path of about 1.6 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b091-v13-19","title":"樓板邊緣、帷幕牆與外牆的垂直蔓延：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Slab edges, curtain walls and vertical spread on the façade: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「帷幕牆層間防火」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Curtain-wall perimeter fire barrier” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"層間防火填塞必須採用與帷幕牆型式一致的試驗系統，現場檢查礦棉密度、壓縮率、支撐角鐵與表面防煙密封，並逐層拍照；外牆材料須有燃燒性能證明，帷幕牆設計審查時把窗間牆與層間填塞一併檢核。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Perimeter fire barriers must be a tested system matching the curtain-wall type, with mineral-wool density, compression, support angles and surface smoke seal inspected and photographed floor by floor; façade materials need combustibility evidence, and curtain-wall design review checks spandrels and perimeter barriers together. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：帷幕牆、防火填塞與結構三方要在施工圖階段協調樓板邊緣細部，層間填塞列為帷幕牆安裝每層的停止點；外牆材料變更必須提出燃燒性證明並經審查，地震後檢查表應包含層間填塞。","observationEn":"Site practice: Curtain-wall, firestopping and structural teams must coordinate slab-edge details at shop-drawing stage, with perimeter barriers a hold point on every floor of curtain-wall installation; any façade material change requires combustibility evidence and review, and post-earthquake checklists should include perimeter barriers.","failure":"注意干擾：層間填塞因帷幕牆變位或施工擠壓脫落，或保溫材被替換為可燃材料，火災時火煙沿樓板邊緣與外牆空腔逐層向上，區劃形同虛設；地震後帷幕牆層間變位也可能把填塞拉開而無人發現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Perimeter barriers dislodged by curtain-wall movement or construction, or insulation swapped for combustible products, let fire and smoke climb floor by floor along slab edges and façade cavities, nullifying compartmentation; storey drift in an earthquake can also pull barriers open unnoticed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"層間防火填塞必須採用與帷幕牆型式一致的試驗系統，現場檢查礦棉密度、壓縮率、支撐角鐵與表面防煙密封，並逐層拍照；外牆材料須有燃燒性能證明，帷幕牆設計審查時把窗間牆與層間填塞一併檢核。","textEn":"Perimeter fire barriers must be a tested system matching the curtain-wall type, with mineral-wool density, compression, support angles and surface smoke seal inspected and photographed floor by floor; façade materials need combustibility evidence, and curtain-wall design review checks spandrels and perimeter barriers together.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"帷幕牆、防火填塞與結構三方要在施工圖階段協調樓板邊緣細部，層間填塞列為帷幕牆安裝每層的停止點；外牆材料變更必須提出燃燒性證明並經審查，地震後檢查表應包含層間填塞。","textEn":"Curtain-wall, firestopping and structural teams must coordinate slab-edge details at shop-drawing stage, with perimeter barriers a hold point on every floor of curtain-wall installation; any façade material change requires combustibility evidence and review, and post-earthquake checklists should include perimeter barriers.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「樓板邊緣、帷幕牆與外牆的垂直蔓延」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Slab edges, curtain walls and vertical spread on the façade\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","層間防火填塞必須採用與帷幕牆型式一致的試驗系統，現場檢查礦棉密度、壓縮率、支撐角鐵與表面防煙密封，並逐層拍照。","防火區劃只是延緩火勢，真正滅火只能靠消防隊，所以區劃不必太嚴格。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Perimeter fire barriers must be a tested system matching the curtain-wall type, with mineral-wool density, compression, support angles and surface smoke seal inspected and photographed floor by floor.","Compartments only delay a fire and only firefighters extinguish it, so compartmentation need not be rigorous."],"answer":1,"explanation":"層間防火填塞必須採用與帷幕牆型式一致的試驗系統，現場檢查礦棉密度、壓縮率、支撐角鐵與表面防煙密封，並逐層拍照；外牆材料須有燃燒性能證明，帷幕牆設計審查時把窗間牆與層間填塞一併檢核。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Perimeter fire barriers must be a tested system matching the curtain-wall type, with mineral-wool density, compression, support angles and surface smoke seal inspected and photographed floor by floor; façade materials need combustibility evidence, and curtain-wall design review checks spandrels and perimeter barriers together. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b091-v13-20","title":"樓板邊緣、帷幕牆與外牆的垂直蔓延：失效診斷","titleEn":"Slab edges, curtain walls and vertical spread on the façade: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「帷幕牆層間防火」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Curtain-wall perimeter fire barrier” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"層間填塞因帷幕牆變位或施工擠壓脫落，或保溫材被替換為可燃材料，火災時火煙沿樓板邊緣與外牆空腔逐層向上，區劃形同虛設；地震後帷幕牆層間變位也可能把填塞拉開而無人發現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Perimeter barriers dislodged by curtain-wall movement or construction, or insulation swapped for combustible products, let fire and smoke climb floor by floor along slab edges and façade cavities, nullifying compartmentation; storey drift in an earthquake can also pull barriers open unnoticed. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計上要同時處理樓板邊緣填塞、窗間牆高度與外牆材料的燃燒性。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Design must address slab-edge firestopping, spandrel height and façade combustibility together.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「樓板本身有防火時效，就代表上下樓層已經完全區劃。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the floor slab is fire-rated, the floors above and below are fully compartmented.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"層間填塞因帷幕牆變位或施工擠壓脫落，或保溫材被替換為可燃材料，火災時火煙沿樓板邊緣與外牆空腔逐層向上，區劃形同虛設；地震後帷幕牆層間變位也可能把填塞拉開而無人發現。","textEn":"Perimeter barriers dislodged by curtain-wall movement or construction, or insulation swapped for combustible products, let fire and smoke climb floor by floor along slab edges and façade cavities, nullifying compartmentation; storey drift in an earthquake can also pull barriers open unnoticed.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「樓板邊緣、帷幕牆與外牆的垂直蔓延」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Slab edges, curtain walls and vertical spread on the façade\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","管線穿過防火牆後，用任何填縫材料補起來就可以。","層間填塞因帷幕牆變位或施工擠壓脫落，或保溫材被替換為可燃材料，火災時火煙沿樓板邊緣與外牆空腔逐層向上，區劃形同虛設。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","After pipes pass through a fire wall, any filler material can seal the gap.","Perimeter barriers dislodged by curtain-wall movement or construction, or insulation swapped for combustible products, let fire and smoke climb floor by floor along slab edges and façade cavities, nullifying compartmentation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"層間填塞因帷幕牆變位或施工擠壓脫落，或保溫材被替換為可燃材料，火災時火煙沿樓板邊緣與外牆空腔逐層向上，區劃形同虛設；地震後帷幕牆層間變位也可能把填塞拉開而無人發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Perimeter barriers dislodged by curtain-wall movement or construction, or insulation swapped for combustible products, let fire and smoke climb floor by floor along slab edges and façade cavities, nullifying compartmentation; storey drift in an earthquake can also pull barriers open unnoticed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b091-v13-21","title":"施工與裝修期間的區劃完整性：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Compartment integrity during construction and fit-out: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「管線貫穿防火填塞」如何影響高層建築消防分區設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Service penetration firestops” governs force, deformation or durability in “Fire compartmentation in high-rise buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"區劃最大的敵人是施工後期與使用期間的穿孔：機電、弱電、空調與消防管線大量穿越區劃牆與樓板，每一個貫穿部都要以與管材、管徑、牆體型式相符的試驗系統封填。許多填塞在區劃牆完成驗收後才被後續工班打開，或以一般發泡材隨意填補。高層建築的貫穿部以萬計，只要少數失效就足以讓煙在樓層間流通。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「管線貫穿防火填塞」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The greatest enemy of compartmentation is late-stage and in-service penetrations: services, data, ductwork and fire-protection pipes cross compartment walls and floors in large numbers, and each penetration must be sealed with a tested system matching pipe material, size and wall type. Many seals are opened by later trades after the wall has been accepted, or patched with ordinary foam. A high-rise building has tens of thousands of penetrations, and a small fraction failing is enough to let smoke circulate between floors. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Service penetration firestops” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：40 層建築每層約 300 個貫穿部，總數 40×300 = 12,000 個；若 2% 未正確封填，即 240 個缺口，每個平均 0.01 m²，等效開口合計約 2.4 m²，分散在各層成為煙的通道。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A 40-storey building with about 300 penetrations per floor has 40×300 = 12,000 in total; if 2% are not properly sealed, 240 gaps averaging 0.01 m² add up to an equivalent opening of about 2.4 m², spread over the floors as smoke paths.","failure":"常見誤解：「管線穿過防火牆後，用任何填縫材料補起來就可以。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"After pipes pass through a fire wall, any filler material can seal the gap.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「管線貫穿防火填塞」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Service penetration firestops”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-21-k1","title":"施工與裝修期間的區劃完整性","titleEn":"Compartment integrity during construction and fit-out","text":"區劃最大的敵人是施工後期與使用期間的穿孔：機電、弱電、空調與消防管線大量穿越區劃牆與樓板，每一個貫穿部都要以與管材、管徑、牆體型式相符的試驗系統封填。許多填塞在區劃牆完成驗收後才被後續工班打開，或以一般發泡材隨意填補。","textEn":"The greatest enemy of compartmentation is late-stage and in-service penetrations: services, data, ductwork and fire-protection pipes cross compartment walls and floors in large numbers, and each penetration must be sealed with a tested system matching pipe material, size and wall type. Many seals are opened by later trades after the wall has been accepted, or patched with ordinary foam.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：管線穿過防火牆後，用任何填縫材料補起來就可以。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: After pipes pass through a fire wall, any filler material can seal the gap. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「施工與裝修期間的區劃完整性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Compartment integrity during construction and fit-out\" is correct?","options":["區劃最大的敵人是施工後期與使用期間的穿孔：機電、弱電、空調與消防管線大量穿越區劃牆與樓板，每一個貫穿部都要以與管材、管徑、牆體型式相符的試驗系統封填。","管線穿過防火牆後，用任何填縫材料補起來就可以。","只要材料本身不燃，組成的牆或門就自動具有防火時效。"],"optionsEn":["The greatest enemy of compartmentation is late-stage and in-service penetrations: services, data, ductwork and fire-protection pipes cross compartment walls and floors in large numbers, and each penetration must be sealed with a tested system matching pipe material, size and wall type.","After pipes pass through a fire wall, any filler material can seal the gap.","If the materials are non-combustible, the wall or door they form automatically has a fire rating."],"answer":0,"explanation":"區劃最大的敵人是施工後期與使用期間的穿孔：機電、弱電、空調與消防管線大量穿越區劃牆與樓板，每一個貫穿部都要以與管材、管徑、牆體型式相符的試驗系統封填。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The greatest enemy of compartmentation is late-stage and in-service penetrations: services, data, ductwork and fire-protection pipes cross compartment walls and floors in large numbers, and each penetration must be sealed with a tested system matching pipe material, size and wall type. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b091-v13-22","title":"施工與裝修期間的區劃完整性：定量估算","titleEn":"Compartment integrity during construction and fit-out: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「管線貫穿防火填塞」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Service penetration firestops” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：40 層建築每層約 300 個貫穿部，總數 40×300 = 12,000 個；若 2% 未正確封填，即 240 個缺口，每個平均 0.01 m²，等效開口合計約 2.4 m²，分散在各層成為煙的通道。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A 40-storey building with about 300 penetrations per floor has 40×300 = 12,000 in total; if 2% are not properly sealed, 240 gaps averaging 0.01 m² add up to an equivalent opening of about 2.4 m², spread over the floors as smoke paths. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立貫穿部登錄系統，每個填塞貼上編號標籤並記錄系統型號、施工人員、日期與照片；由獨立檢查人員抽樣破壞性或目視檢查，發現缺失即擴大抽查；區劃牆在天花板封板前設停止點，未完成填塞不得封板。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Set up a penetration register in which each seal carries a numbered label recording system, installer, date and photograph; an independent inspector samples seals visually or destructively and extends sampling when defects appear; compartment walls have a hold point before ceilings close, and no ceiling may close over incomplete seals.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"40 層建築每層約 300 個貫穿部，總數 40×300 = 12,000 個；若 2% 未正確封填，即 240 個缺口，每個平均 0.01 m²，等效開口合計約 2.4 m²，分散在各層成為煙的通道。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A 40-storey building with about 300 penetrations per floor has 40×300 = 12,000 in total; if 2% are not properly sealed, 240 gaps averaging 0.01 m² add up to an equivalent opening of about 2.4 m², spread over the floors as smoke paths. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「施工與裝修期間的區劃完整性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Compartment integrity during construction and fit-out\", which statement holds?","options":["鋼構只要有防火被覆，區劃失效也不會影響結構安全。","40 層建築每層約 300 個貫穿部，總數 40×300 = 12,000 個。","只要設了灑水系統，防火區劃就可有可無。"],"optionsEn":["Steelwork with fireproofing is safe even if compartmentation fails.","A 40-storey building with about 300 penetrations per floor has 40×300 = 12,000 in total.","With sprinklers installed, compartmentation is optional."],"answer":1,"explanation":"40 層建築每層約 300 個貫穿部，總數 40×300 = 12,000 個；若 2% 未正確封填，即 240 個缺口，每個平均 0.01 m²，等效開口合計約 2.4 m²，分散在各層成為煙的通道。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A 40-storey building with about 300 penetrations per floor has 40×300 = 12,000 in total; if 2% are not properly sealed, 240 gaps averaging 0.01 m² add up to an equivalent opening of about 2.4 m², spread over the floors as smoke paths. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b091-v13-23","title":"施工與裝修期間的區劃完整性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Compartment integrity during construction and fit-out: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「管線貫穿防火填塞」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Service penetration firestops” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立貫穿部登錄系統，每個填塞貼上編號標籤並記錄系統型號、施工人員、日期與照片；由獨立檢查人員抽樣破壞性或目視檢查，發現缺失即擴大抽查；區劃牆在天花板封板前設停止點，未完成填塞不得封板。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Set up a penetration register in which each seal carries a numbered label recording system, installer, date and photograph; an independent inspector samples seals visually or destructively and extends sampling when defects appear; compartment walls have a hold point before ceilings close, and no ceiling may close over incomplete seals. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：施工規範規定區劃上的任何新開孔須先申請許可並指定合格施工者，完工後更新登錄系統；物業管理階段沿用同一套許可制度，裝修承包商退場前由管理單位檢查區劃。","observationEn":"Site practice: The specification requires a permit and a qualified installer for any new opening in a compartment, with the register updated afterwards; the same permit system continues in facility management, and managers inspect compartments before fit-out contractors leave.","failure":"注意干擾：後續工班為了新增線路在已填塞的貫穿部旁鑿孔，事後只用一般矽利康或發泡劑封住，外觀看似完整，火災時這些材料迅速燒失，煙與火穿過區劃；天花板封閉後無人再檢查，缺陷一直潛伏到火災發生。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Later trades break through beside sealed penetrations to add cables and close them with ordinary sealant or foam; it looks complete, but in a fire these materials burn away quickly and smoke and flame pass through, and once ceilings close nobody checks again until a fire reveals the defect. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立貫穿部登錄系統，每個填塞貼上編號標籤並記錄系統型號、施工人員、日期與照片；由獨立檢查人員抽樣破壞性或目視檢查，發現缺失即擴大抽查；區劃牆在天花板封板前設停止點，未完成填塞不得封板。","textEn":"Set up a penetration register in which each seal carries a numbered label recording system, installer, date and photograph; an independent inspector samples seals visually or destructively and extends sampling when defects appear; compartment walls have a hold point before ceilings close, and no ceiling may close over incomplete seals.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"施工規範規定區劃上的任何新開孔須先申請許可並指定合格施工者，完工後更新登錄系統；物業管理階段沿用同一套許可制度，裝修承包商退場前由管理單位檢查區劃。","textEn":"The specification requires a permit and a qualified installer for any new opening in a compartment, with the register updated afterwards; the same permit system continues in facility management, and managers inspect compartments before fit-out contractors leave.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「施工與裝修期間的區劃完整性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Compartment integrity during construction and fit-out\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","標示一小時防火時效的牆，在任何火災中都一定能撐一小時。","建立貫穿部登錄系統，每個填塞貼上編號標籤並記錄系統型號、施工人員、日期與照片。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A wall rated for one hour will always last one hour in any fire.","Set up a penetration register in which each seal carries a numbered label recording system, installer, date and photograph."],"answer":2,"explanation":"建立貫穿部登錄系統，每個填塞貼上編號標籤並記錄系統型號、施工人員、日期與照片；由獨立檢查人員抽樣破壞性或目視檢查，發現缺失即擴大抽查；區劃牆在天花板封板前設停止點，未完成填塞不得封板。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Set up a penetration register in which each seal carries a numbered label recording system, installer, date and photograph; an independent inspector samples seals visually or destructively and extends sampling when defects appear; compartment walls have a hold point before ceilings close, and no ceiling may close over incomplete seals. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b091-v13-24","title":"施工與裝修期間的區劃完整性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Compartment integrity during construction and fit-out: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「管線貫穿防火填塞」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Service penetration firestops” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"後續工班為了新增線路在已填塞的貫穿部旁鑿孔，事後只用一般矽利康或發泡劑封住，外觀看似完整，火災時這些材料迅速燒失，煙與火穿過區劃；天花板封閉後無人再檢查，缺陷一直潛伏到火災發生。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Later trades break through beside sealed penetrations to add cables and close them with ordinary sealant or foam; it looks complete, but in a fire these materials burn away quickly and smoke and flame pass through, and once ceilings close nobody checks again until a fire reveals the defect. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：高層建築的貫穿部以萬計，只要少數失效就足以讓煙在樓層間流通。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A high-rise building has tens of thousands of penetrations, and a small fraction failing is enough to let smoke circulate between floors.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「管線穿過防火牆後，用任何填縫材料補起來就可以。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"After pipes pass through a fire wall, any filler material can seal the gap.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"後續工班為了新增線路在已填塞的貫穿部旁鑿孔，事後只用一般矽利康或發泡劑封住，外觀看似完整，火災時這些材料迅速燒失，煙與火穿過區劃；天花板封閉後無人再檢查，缺陷一直潛伏到火災發生。","textEn":"Later trades break through beside sealed penetrations to add cables and close them with ordinary sealant or foam; it looks complete, but in a fire these materials burn away quickly and smoke and flame pass through, and once ceilings close nobody checks again until a fire reveals the defect.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「施工與裝修期間的區劃完整性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Compartment integrity during construction and fit-out\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["後續工班為了新增線路在已填塞的貫穿部旁鑿孔，事後只用一般矽利康或發泡劑封住，外觀看似完整，火災時這些材料迅速燒失，煙與火穿過區劃。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","只要材料本身不燃，組成的牆或門就自動具有防火時效。"],"optionsEn":["Later trades break through beside sealed penetrations to add cables and close them with ordinary sealant or foam.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","If the materials are non-combustible, the wall or door they form automatically has a fire rating."],"answer":0,"explanation":"後續工班為了新增線路在已填塞的貫穿部旁鑿孔，事後只用一般矽利康或發泡劑封住，外觀看似完整，火災時這些材料迅速燒失，煙與火穿過區劃；天花板封閉後無人再檢查，缺陷一直潛伏到火災發生。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Later trades break through beside sealed penetrations to add cables and close them with ordinary sealant or foam; it looks complete, but in a fire these materials burn away quickly and smoke and flame pass through, and once ceilings close nobody checks again until a fire reveals the defect. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b091-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「耐火試驗、判定準則與認可範圍」與「樓梯加壓、排煙與驗收試驗」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Fire-resistance tests, criteria and scope of approval\" and \"Stair pressurisation, smoke control and acceptance tests\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b091-v13-25","title":"耐火試驗、判定準則與認可範圍：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Fire-resistance tests, criteria and scope of approval: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「標準耐火試驗爐」如何影響高層建築消防分區設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Standard fire-resistance furnace” governs force, deformation or durability in “Fire compartmentation in high-rise buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"區劃構件的防火時效來自標準耐火試驗：把牆、樓板、門或貫穿系統安裝在試驗爐上，依 ISO 834、ASTM E119 或國家標準的升溫曲線加熱，觀察承載力、完整性（有無火焰穿透或棉墊點燃）與隔熱性（背火面平均溫升與最高點溫升）何時失效。試驗結果只適用於試驗構造及其認可的延伸範圍，尺寸、材料、固定方式與試驗不同時，不能直接沿用。台灣內政部建築研究所等機構設有性能試驗設施，支持防火材料與構造的驗證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「標準耐火試驗爐」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An element's fire rating comes from standard fire-resistance tests: a wall, floor, door or penetration system is mounted on a furnace and heated to the ISO 834, ASTM E119 or national curve while load-bearing capacity, integrity (flame penetration or cotton-pad ignition) and insulation (average and maximum temperature rise on the unexposed face) are watched for failure. Results apply only to the tested construction and its approved field of extension; different sizes, materials or fixings cannot simply borrow the rating. Institutions such as Taiwan's Architecture and Building Research Institute operate performance test facilities that support verification of fire-resisting materials and constructions. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Standard fire-resistance furnace” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：ISO 834 曲線 30 min 時約 842°C、60 min 約 945°C。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The ISO 834 curve reaches about 842°C at 30 min and 945°C at 60 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要材料本身不燃，組成的牆或門就自動具有防火時效。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the materials are non-combustible, the wall or door they form automatically has a fire rating.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「標準耐火試驗爐」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Standard fire-resistance furnace”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-25-k1","title":"耐火試驗、判定準則與認可範圍","titleEn":"Fire-resistance tests, criteria and scope of approval","text":"區劃構件的防火時效來自標準耐火試驗：把牆、樓板、門或貫穿系統安裝在試驗爐上，依 ISO 834、ASTM E119 或國家標準的升溫曲線加熱，觀察承載力、完整性（有無火焰穿透或棉墊點燃）與隔熱性（背火面平均溫升與最高點溫升）何時失效。試驗結果只適用於試驗構造及其認可的延伸範圍，尺寸、材料、固定方式與試驗不同時，不能直接沿用。","textEn":"An element's fire rating comes from standard fire-resistance tests: a wall, floor, door or penetration system is mounted on a furnace and heated to the ISO 834, ASTM E119 or national curve while load-bearing capacity, integrity (flame penetration or cotton-pad ignition) and insulation (average and maximum temperature rise on the unexposed face) are watched for failure. Results apply only to the tested construction and its approved field of extension; different sizes, materials or fixings cannot simply borrow the rating.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要材料本身不燃，組成的牆或門就自動具有防火時效。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the materials are non-combustible, the wall or door they form automatically has a fire rating. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「耐火試驗、判定準則與認可範圍」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fire-resistance tests, criteria and scope of approval\" is correct?","options":["只要材料本身不燃，組成的牆或門就自動具有防火時效。","區劃構件的防火時效來自標準耐火試驗：把牆、樓板、門或貫穿系統安裝在試驗爐上，依 ISO 834、ASTM E119 或國家標準的升溫曲線加熱，觀察承載力、完整性（有無火焰穿透或棉墊點燃）與隔熱性（背火面平均溫升與最高點溫升）何時失效。","樓梯加壓的壓力越大越安全。"],"optionsEn":["If the materials are non-combustible, the wall or door they form automatically has a fire rating.","An element's fire rating comes from standard fire-resistance tests: a wall, floor, door or penetration system is mounted on a furnace and heated to the ISO 834, ASTM E119 or national curve while load-bearing capacity, integrity (flame penetration or cotton-pad ignition) and insulation (average and maximum temperature rise on the unexposed face) are watched for failure.","The higher the stair pressurisation, the safer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"區劃構件的防火時效來自標準耐火試驗：把牆、樓板、門或貫穿系統安裝在試驗爐上，依 ISO 834、ASTM E119 或國家標準的升溫曲線加熱，觀察承載力、完整性（有無火焰穿透或棉墊點燃）與隔熱性（背火面平均溫升與最高點溫升）何時失效。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An element's fire rating comes from standard fire-resistance tests: a wall, floor, door or penetration system is mounted on a furnace and heated to the ISO 834, ASTM E119 or national curve while load-bearing capacity, integrity (flame penetration or cotton-pad ignition) and insulation (average and maximum temperature rise on the unexposed face) are watched for failure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b091-v13-26","title":"耐火試驗、判定準則與認可範圍：定量估算","titleEn":"Fire-resistance tests, criteria and scope of approval: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「標準耐火試驗爐」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Standard fire-resistance furnace” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：ISO 834 曲線 30 min 時約 842°C、60 min 約 945°C。隔熱性常以背火面平均溫升不超過 140 K、任一點不超過 180 K 判定：室溫 20°C 時，背火面平均溫度達 160°C 或任一點達 200°C 即判定隔熱失效；若 52 分鐘時平均溫度先達 160°C，該構造只能認定為 30 分鐘等級而非 60 分鐘。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The ISO 834 curve reaches about 842°C at 30 min and 945°C at 60 min. Insulation is commonly judged by an average unexposed-face rise of no more than 140 K and no more than 180 K at any point: from 20°C ambient, failure occurs when the average reaches 160°C or any point reaches 200°C; if the average hits 160°C at 52 minutes, the construction rates only 30 minutes, not 60. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：審查試驗報告時核對試驗標準、試體尺寸、構造層次、固定方式、承載狀態與失效時間，並確認認可範圍涵蓋現場尺寸與配置；必要時要求第三方認證機構的產品認證與工廠品質管制紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: When reviewing test reports, check the standard, specimen size, build-up, fixing, loading condition and failure times, and confirm that the approved scope covers site sizes and configurations; where needed require third-party product certification and factory quality-control records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"ISO 834 曲線 30 min 時約 842°C、60 min 約 945°C。隔熱性常以背火面平均溫升不超過 140 K、任一點不超過 180 K 判定：室溫 20°C 時，背火面平均溫度達 160°C 或任一點達 200°C 即判定隔熱失效；若 52 分鐘時平均溫度先達 160°C，該構造只能認定為 30 分鐘等級而非 60 分鐘。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The ISO 834 curve reaches about 842°C at 30 min and 945°C at 60 min. Insulation is commonly judged by an average unexposed-face rise of no more than 140 K and no more than 180 K at any point: from 20°C ambient, failure occurs when the average reaches 160°C or any point reaches 200°C; if the average hits 160°C at 52 minutes, the construction rates only 30 minutes, not 60. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「耐火試驗、判定準則與認可範圍」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fire-resistance tests, criteria and scope of approval\", which statement holds?","options":["老舊建築只要當年合法取得使用執照，就不需要再檢討防火區劃。","防火區劃只是延緩火勢，真正滅火只能靠消防隊，所以區劃不必太嚴格。","ISO 834 曲線 30 min 時約 842°C、60 min 約 945°C。"],"optionsEn":["An old building that was lawfully approved when built needs no further review of its compartmentation.","Compartments only delay a fire and only firefighters extinguish it, so compartmentation need not be rigorous.","The ISO 834 curve reaches about 842°C at 30 min and 945°C at 60 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"ISO 834 曲線 30 min 時約 842°C、60 min 約 945°C。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The ISO 834 curve reaches about 842°C at 30 min and 945°C at 60 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b091-v13-27","title":"耐火試驗、判定準則與認可範圍：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fire-resistance tests, criteria and scope of approval: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「標準耐火試驗爐」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Standard fire-resistance furnace” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"審查試驗報告時核對試驗標準、試體尺寸、構造層次、固定方式、承載狀態與失效時間，並確認認可範圍涵蓋現場尺寸與配置；必要時要求第三方認證機構的產品認證與工廠品質管制紀錄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"When reviewing test reports, check the standard, specimen size, build-up, fixing, loading condition and failure times, and confirm that the approved scope covers site sizes and configurations; where needed require third-party product certification and factory quality-control records. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：設計說明應明列每種防火構造引用的試驗報告編號與認可範圍，承包商變更產品須提出同等或更佳的試驗證明並經建築師與消防審查核可。","observationEn":"Site practice: The design basis should list the test report number and approved scope for each fire-resisting construction, and any product substitution by the contractor must be supported by equal or better test evidence and approved by the architect and fire reviewer.","failure":"注意干擾：若引用的試驗報告是較小尺寸的門或較薄的牆，現場大尺寸構造在火災中翹曲變形、提早出現縫隙；把非承重試驗的牆當作承重區劃牆使用，火災中可能因承載而提早倒塌。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Citing a test on a smaller door or thinner wall means larger site constructions bow and open gaps early in a fire; using a wall tested as non-load-bearing as a load-bearing compartment wall can lead to early collapse under load in a fire. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"審查試驗報告時核對試驗標準、試體尺寸、構造層次、固定方式、承載狀態與失效時間，並確認認可範圍涵蓋現場尺寸與配置；必要時要求第三方認證機構的產品認證與工廠品質管制紀錄。","textEn":"When reviewing test reports, check the standard, specimen size, build-up, fixing, loading condition and failure times, and confirm that the approved scope covers site sizes and configurations; where needed require third-party product certification and factory quality-control records.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"設計說明應明列每種防火構造引用的試驗報告編號與認可範圍，承包商變更產品須提出同等或更佳的試驗證明並經建築師與消防審查核可。","textEn":"The design basis should list the test report number and approved scope for each fire-resisting construction, and any product substitution by the contractor must be supported by equal or better test evidence and approved by the architect and fire reviewer.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「耐火試驗、判定準則與認可範圍」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fire-resistance tests, criteria and scope of approval\"?","options":["審查試驗報告時核對試驗標準、試體尺寸、構造層次、固定方式、承載狀態與失效時間，並確認認可範圍涵蓋現場尺寸與配置。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","防火門只要是防火材料做的，開著也能擋火。"],"optionsEn":["When reviewing test reports, check the standard, specimen size, build-up, fixing, loading condition and failure times, and confirm that the approved scope covers site sizes and configurations.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A fire door made of fire-resisting material still stops fire when left open."],"answer":0,"explanation":"審查試驗報告時核對試驗標準、試體尺寸、構造層次、固定方式、承載狀態與失效時間，並確認認可範圍涵蓋現場尺寸與配置；必要時要求第三方認證機構的產品認證與工廠品質管制紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"When reviewing test reports, check the standard, specimen size, build-up, fixing, loading condition and failure times, and confirm that the approved scope covers site sizes and configurations; where needed require third-party product certification and factory quality-control records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b091-v13-28","title":"耐火試驗、判定準則與認可範圍：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fire-resistance tests, criteria and scope of approval: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「標準耐火試驗爐」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Standard fire-resistance furnace” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若引用的試驗報告是較小尺寸的門或較薄的牆，現場大尺寸構造在火災中翹曲變形、提早出現縫隙；把非承重試驗的牆當作承重區劃牆使用，火災中可能因承載而提早倒塌。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Citing a test on a smaller door or thinner wall means larger site constructions bow and open gaps early in a fire; using a wall tested as non-load-bearing as a load-bearing compartment wall can lead to early collapse under load in a fire. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：台灣內政部建築研究所等機構設有性能試驗設施，支持防火材料與構造的驗證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Institutions such as Taiwan's Architecture and Building Research Institute operate performance test facilities that support verification of fire-resisting materials and constructions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要材料本身不燃，組成的牆或門就自動具有防火時效。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the materials are non-combustible, the wall or door they form automatically has a fire rating.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若引用的試驗報告是較小尺寸的門或較薄的牆，現場大尺寸構造在火災中翹曲變形、提早出現縫隙；把非承重試驗的牆當作承重區劃牆使用，火災中可能因承載而提早倒塌。","textEn":"Citing a test on a smaller door or thinner wall means larger site constructions bow and open gaps early in a fire; using a wall tested as non-load-bearing as a load-bearing compartment wall can lead to early collapse under load in a fire.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「耐火試驗、判定準則與認可範圍」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fire-resistance tests, criteria and scope of approval\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若引用的試驗報告是較小尺寸的門或較薄的牆，現場大尺寸構造在火災中翹曲變形、提早出現縫隙；把非承重試驗的牆當作承重區劃牆使用，火災中可能因承載而提早倒塌。","樓梯加壓的壓力越大越安全。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Citing a test on a smaller door or thinner wall means larger site constructions bow and open gaps early in a fire.","The higher the stair pressurisation, the safer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若引用的試驗報告是較小尺寸的門或較薄的牆，現場大尺寸構造在火災中翹曲變形、提早出現縫隙；把非承重試驗的牆當作承重區劃牆使用，火災中可能因承載而提早倒塌。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Citing a test on a smaller door or thinner wall means larger site constructions bow and open gaps early in a fire; using a wall tested as non-load-bearing as a load-bearing compartment wall can lead to early collapse under load in a fire. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b091-v13-29","title":"樓梯加壓、排煙與驗收試驗：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Stair pressurisation, smoke control and acceptance tests: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「特別安全梯加壓」如何影響高層建築消防分區設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Stair pressurisation” governs force, deformation or durability in “Fire compartmentation in high-rise buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"高層建築的樓梯與緊急昇降機間是垂直逃生與消防搶救的生命線，常以加壓送風維持比走廊高的壓力，讓門縫只往外漏氣而不讓煙進入。但壓力太高時，門會推不開，避難者無法進入樓梯；壓力太低則擋不住煙。煙囪效應使高層建築上下壓力分布不同，冬夏也不一樣，因此加壓系統要在實際建築中做驗收試驗，確認多扇門同時開啟時仍能維持壓差，且開門力在限值內。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「特別安全梯加壓」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Stairs and fire-fighting lift lobbies in tall buildings are the lifelines for vertical escape and firefighting, often pressurised above corridor pressure so that air leaks outward through door gaps and smoke stays out. Too much pressure makes doors impossible to open and occupants cannot enter the stair; too little fails to hold back smoke. Stack effect distributes pressure differently over the height and between winter and summer, so pressurisation must be acceptance-tested in the real building to confirm that the pressure difference holds with several doors open and that door-opening forces stay within limits. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Stair pressurisation” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：開門力 F = F_dc + W·A·ΔP/[2(W − d)]。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Door-opening force F = F_dc + W·A·ΔP/[2(W − d)].","failure":"常見誤解：「樓梯加壓的壓力越大越安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The higher the stair pressurisation, the safer.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「特別安全梯加壓」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Stair pressurisation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-29-k1","title":"樓梯加壓、排煙與驗收試驗","titleEn":"Stair pressurisation, smoke control and acceptance tests","text":"高層建築的樓梯與緊急昇降機間是垂直逃生與消防搶救的生命線，常以加壓送風維持比走廊高的壓力，讓門縫只往外漏氣而不讓煙進入。但壓力太高時，門會推不開，避難者無法進入樓梯；壓力太低則擋不住煙。","textEn":"Stairs and fire-fighting lift lobbies in tall buildings are the lifelines for vertical escape and firefighting, often pressurised above corridor pressure so that air leaks outward through door gaps and smoke stays out. Too much pressure makes doors impossible to open and occupants cannot enter the stair; too little fails to hold back smoke.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：樓梯加壓的壓力越大越安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The higher the stair pressurisation, the safer. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「樓梯加壓、排煙與驗收試驗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stair pressurisation, smoke control and acceptance tests\" is correct?","options":["樓梯加壓的壓力越大越安全。","鋼構只要有防火被覆，區劃失效也不會影響結構安全。","高層建築的樓梯與緊急昇降機間是垂直逃生與消防搶救的生命線，常以加壓送風維持比走廊高的壓力，讓門縫只往外漏氣而不讓煙進入。"],"optionsEn":["The higher the stair pressurisation, the safer.","Steelwork with fireproofing is safe even if compartmentation fails.","Stairs and fire-fighting lift lobbies in tall buildings are the lifelines for vertical escape and firefighting, often pressurised above corridor pressure so that air leaks outward through door gaps and smoke stays out."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高層建築的樓梯與緊急昇降機間是垂直逃生與消防搶救的生命線，常以加壓送風維持比走廊高的壓力，讓門縫只往外漏氣而不讓煙進入。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Stairs and fire-fighting lift lobbies in tall buildings are the lifelines for vertical escape and firefighting, often pressurised above corridor pressure so that air leaks outward through door gaps and smoke stays out. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b091-v13-30","title":"樓梯加壓、排煙與驗收試驗：定量估算","titleEn":"Stair pressurisation, smoke control and acceptance tests: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「特別安全梯加壓」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Stair pressurisation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：開門力 F = F_dc + W·A·ΔP/[2(W − d)]。門寬 W = 0.9 m、門面積 A = 1.89 m²、把手距門邊 d = 0.075 m、門弓器力 F_dc = 40 N：ΔP = 50 Pa 時 F = 40 + 0.9×1.89×50/(2×0.825) ≈ 91.5 N；ΔP = 80 Pa 時約 122.5 N，接近常見的 133 N 上限。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Door-opening force F = F_dc + W·A·ΔP/[2(W − d)]. With door width W = 0.9 m, area A = 1.89 m², knob distance d = 0.075 m and closer force F_dc = 40 N: at ΔP = 50 Pa, F = 40 + 0.9×1.89×50/(2×0.825) ≈ 91.5 N; at 80 Pa about 122.5 N, close to the common 133 N limit. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：驗收時在多個樓層量測樓梯與走廊間的壓差，分別在全部門關閉與指定數量門開啟時測試，並以拉力計量測開門力；夏季與冬季各測一次以涵蓋煙囪效應，結果與設計值比較並記錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: At acceptance, measure pressure difference between stair and corridor on several floors with all doors closed and with the specified number of doors open, and measure door-opening force with a force gauge; test in both summer and winter to capture stack effect, recording results against design values.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"開門力 F = F_dc + W·A·ΔP/[2(W − d)]。門寬 W = 0.9 m、門面積 A = 1.89 m²、把手距門邊 d = 0.075 m、門弓器力 F_dc = 40 N：ΔP = 50 Pa 時 F = 40 + 0.9×1.89×50/(2×0.825) ≈ 91.5 N；ΔP = 80 Pa 時約 122.5 N，接近常見的 133 N 上限。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Door-opening force F = F_dc + W·A·ΔP/[2(W − d)]. With door width W = 0.9 m, area A = 1.89 m², knob distance d = 0.075 m and closer force F_dc = 40 N: at ΔP = 50 Pa, F = 40 + 0.9×1.89×50/(2×0.825) ≈ 91.5 N; at 80 Pa about 122.5 N, close to the common 133 N limit. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「樓梯加壓、排煙與驗收試驗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stair pressurisation, smoke control and acceptance tests\", which statement holds?","options":["開門力 F = F_dc + W·A·ΔP/[2(W − d)]。","只要設了灑水系統，防火區劃就可有可無。","標示一小時防火時效的牆，在任何火災中都一定能撐一小時。"],"optionsEn":["Door-opening force F = F_dc + W·A·ΔP/[2(W − d)].","With sprinklers installed, compartmentation is optional.","A wall rated for one hour will always last one hour in any fire."],"answer":0,"explanation":"開門力 F = F_dc + W·A·ΔP/[2(W − d)]。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Door-opening force F = F_dc + W·A·ΔP/[2(W − d)]. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b091-v13-31","title":"樓梯加壓、排煙與驗收試驗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stair pressurisation, smoke control and acceptance tests: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「特別安全梯加壓」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stair pressurisation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"驗收時在多個樓層量測樓梯與走廊間的壓差，分別在全部門關閉與指定數量門開啟時測試，並以拉力計量測開門力；夏季與冬季各測一次以涵蓋煙囪效應，結果與設計值比較並記錄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"At acceptance, measure pressure difference between stair and corridor on several floors with all doors closed and with the specified number of doors open, and measure door-opening force with a force gauge; test in both summer and winter to capture stack effect, recording results against design values. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：加壓與排煙系統的驗收應包含跨季節試驗與聯動測試，並納入年度消防安全設備檢修；任何樓梯門、走廊隔間或機電改裝後，須重新量測壓差與開門力。","observationEn":"Site practice: Acceptance of pressurisation and smoke control should include seasonal and interlock tests and be part of annual fire-protection maintenance; after any change to stair doors, corridor partitions or services, re-measure pressure difference and door-opening force.","failure":"注意干擾：若只在單一樓層、單一季節測試，冬季強烈煙囪效應下低樓層門可能推不開，高樓層壓差卻不足而進煙；加壓風機的電源與偵測連動若未與區劃同步維護，火災時加壓失效，樓梯成為煙囪。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Testing on one floor in one season can miss that, under strong winter stack effect, lower-floor doors cannot be opened while upper floors lack pressure and admit smoke; if fan power and detector interlocks are not maintained along with compartments, pressurisation fails in a fire and the stair becomes a chimney. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"驗收時在多個樓層量測樓梯與走廊間的壓差，分別在全部門關閉與指定數量門開啟時測試，並以拉力計量測開門力；夏季與冬季各測一次以涵蓋煙囪效應，結果與設計值比較並記錄。","textEn":"At acceptance, measure pressure difference between stair and corridor on several floors with all doors closed and with the specified number of doors open, and measure door-opening force with a force gauge; test in both summer and winter to capture stack effect, recording results against design values.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"加壓與排煙系統的驗收應包含跨季節試驗與聯動測試，並納入年度消防安全設備檢修；任何樓梯門、走廊隔間或機電改裝後，須重新量測壓差與開門力。","textEn":"Acceptance of pressurisation and smoke control should include seasonal and interlock tests and be part of annual fire-protection maintenance; after any change to stair doors, corridor partitions or services, re-measure pressure difference and door-opening force.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「樓梯加壓、排煙與驗收試驗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stair pressurisation, smoke control and acceptance tests\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","驗收時在多個樓層量測樓梯與走廊間的壓差，分別在全部門關閉與指定數量門開啟時測試，並以拉力計量測開門力；夏季與冬季各測一次以涵蓋煙囪效應，結果與設計值比較並記錄。","樓板本身有防火時效，就代表上下樓層已經完全區劃。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","At acceptance, measure pressure difference between stair and corridor on several floors with all doors closed and with the specified number of doors open, and measure door-opening force with a force gauge.","If the floor slab is fire-rated, the floors above and below are fully compartmented."],"answer":1,"explanation":"驗收時在多個樓層量測樓梯與走廊間的壓差，分別在全部門關閉與指定數量門開啟時測試，並以拉力計量測開門力；夏季與冬季各測一次以涵蓋煙囪效應，結果與設計值比較並記錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"At acceptance, measure pressure difference between stair and corridor on several floors with all doors closed and with the specified number of doors open, and measure door-opening force with a force gauge; test in both summer and winter to capture stack effect, recording results against design values. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b091-v13-32","title":"樓梯加壓、排煙與驗收試驗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stair pressurisation, smoke control and acceptance tests: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「特別安全梯加壓」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Stair pressurisation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只在單一樓層、單一季節測試，冬季強烈煙囪效應下低樓層門可能推不開，高樓層壓差卻不足而進煙；加壓風機的電源與偵測連動若未與區劃同步維護，火災時加壓失效，樓梯成為煙囪。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Testing on one floor in one season can miss that, under strong winter stack effect, lower-floor doors cannot be opened while upper floors lack pressure and admit smoke; if fan power and detector interlocks are not maintained along with compartments, pressurisation fails in a fire and the stair becomes a chimney. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：煙囪效應使高層建築上下壓力分布不同，冬夏也不一樣，因此加壓系統要在實際建築中做驗收試驗，確認多扇門同時開啟時仍能維持壓差，且開門力在限值內。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Stack effect distributes pressure differently over the height and between winter and summer, so pressurisation must be acceptance-tested in the real building to confirm that the pressure difference holds with several doors open and that door-opening forces stay within limits.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「樓梯加壓的壓力越大越安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The higher the stair pressurisation, the safer.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只在單一樓層、單一季節測試，冬季強烈煙囪效應下低樓層門可能推不開，高樓層壓差卻不足而進煙；加壓風機的電源與偵測連動若未與區劃同步維護，火災時加壓失效，樓梯成為煙囪。","textEn":"Testing on one floor in one season can miss that, under strong winter stack effect, lower-floor doors cannot be opened while upper floors lack pressure and admit smoke; if fan power and detector interlocks are not maintained along with compartments, pressurisation fails in a fire and the stair becomes a chimney.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「樓梯加壓、排煙與驗收試驗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stair pressurisation, smoke control and acceptance tests\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","鋼構只要有防火被覆，區劃失效也不會影響結構安全。","若只在單一樓層、單一季節測試，冬季強烈煙囪效應下低樓層門可能推不開，高樓層壓差卻不足而進煙。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Steelwork with fireproofing is safe even if compartmentation fails.","Testing on one floor in one season can miss that, under strong winter stack effect, lower-floor doors cannot be opened while upper floors lack pressure and admit smoke."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若只在單一樓層、單一季節測試，冬季強烈煙囪效應下低樓層門可能推不開，高樓層壓差卻不足而進煙；加壓風機的電源與偵測連動若未與區劃同步維護，火災時加壓失效，樓梯成為煙囪。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Testing on one floor in one season can miss that, under strong winter stack effect, lower-floor doors cannot be opened while upper floors lack pressure and admit smoke; if fan power and detector interlocks are not maintained along with compartments, pressurisation fails in a fire and the stair becomes a chimney. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b091-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「區劃失效時的結構防火」與「使用管理、避難時間與交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Structural fire safety when compartments fail\" and \"Management in use, escape time and handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b091-v13-33","title":"區劃失效時的結構防火：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Structural fire safety when compartments fail: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「鋼構臨界溫度」如何影響高層建築消防分區設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Steel critical temperature” governs force, deformation or durability in “Fire compartmentation in high-rise buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"區劃假設火災被限制在一個區劃內燒完，結構防火被覆也依此設計；若灑水與區劃同時失效，多個區劃或多層同時燃燒，熱膨脹與強度折減會同時作用在大範圍的梁、柱與接頭上。One Meridian Plaza 火災後鋼梁與大梁下垂扭曲、樓板開裂，世界貿易中心 7 號大樓則在下層火災失控後倒塌。結構工程師要知道構件在多高的溫度會失去承載力，並與防火被覆的設計溫度一致。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「鋼構臨界溫度」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compartmentation assumes a fire burns out within one compartment, and structural fire protection is designed accordingly; if sprinklers and compartments both fail, several compartments or floors burn at once, and thermal expansion and strength loss act together on beams, columns and connections over a wide area. After the One Meridian Plaza fire, steel beams and girders sagged and twisted and floors cracked, while World Trade Center 7 collapsed after lower-floor fires burned uncontrolled. Structural engineers must know the temperature at which members lose capacity and align it with the fireproofing design temperature. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Steel critical temperature” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：EN 1993-1-2 臨界溫度 θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The EN 1993-1-2 critical temperature is θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼構只要有防火被覆，區劃失效也不會影響結構安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Steelwork with fireproofing is safe even if compartmentation fails.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「鋼構臨界溫度」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Steel critical temperature”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-33-k1","title":"區劃失效時的結構防火","titleEn":"Structural fire safety when compartments fail","text":"區劃假設火災被限制在一個區劃內燒完，結構防火被覆也依此設計；若灑水與區劃同時失效，多個區劃或多層同時燃燒，熱膨脹與強度折減會同時作用在大範圍的梁、柱與接頭上。One Meridian Plaza 火災後鋼梁與大梁下垂扭曲、樓板開裂，世界貿易中心 7 號大樓則在下層火災失控後倒塌。","textEn":"Compartmentation assumes a fire burns out within one compartment, and structural fire protection is designed accordingly; if sprinklers and compartments both fail, several compartments or floors burn at once, and thermal expansion and strength loss act together on beams, columns and connections over a wide area. After the One Meridian Plaza fire, steel beams and girders sagged and twisted and floors cracked, while World Trade Center 7 collapsed after lower-floor fires burned uncontrolled.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼構只要有防火被覆，區劃失效也不會影響結構安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Steelwork with fireproofing is safe even if compartmentation fails. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「區劃失效時的結構防火」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Structural fire safety when compartments fail\" is correct?","options":["區劃假設火災被限制在一個區劃內燒完，結構防火被覆也依此設計；若灑水與區劃同時失效，多個區劃或多層同時燃燒，熱膨脹與強度折減會同時作用在大範圍的梁、柱與接頭上。","鋼構只要有防火被覆，區劃失效也不會影響結構安全。","老舊建築只要當年合法取得使用執照，就不需要再檢討防火區劃。"],"optionsEn":["Compartmentation assumes a fire burns out within one compartment, and structural fire protection is designed accordingly.","Steelwork with fireproofing is safe even if compartmentation fails.","An old building that was lawfully approved when built needs no further review of its compartmentation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"區劃假設火災被限制在一個區劃內燒完，結構防火被覆也依此設計；若灑水與區劃同時失效，多個區劃或多層同時燃燒，熱膨脹與強度折減會同時作用在大範圍的梁、柱與接頭上。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compartmentation assumes a fire burns out within one compartment, and structural fire protection is designed accordingly; if sprinklers and compartments both fail, several compartments or floors burn at once, and thermal expansion and strength loss act together on beams, columns and connections over a wide area. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b091-v13-34","title":"區劃失效時的結構防火：定量估算","titleEn":"Structural fire safety when compartments fail: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼構臨界溫度」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Steel critical temperature” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：EN 1993-1-2 臨界溫度 θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482。使用率 μ₀ = 0.5 時 θ_cr ≈ 585°C；μ₀ = 0.7 時降為約 526°C；μ₀ = 0.3 時升為約 664°C。使用率越高，允許的鋼材溫度越低，防火被覆要越厚。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The EN 1993-1-2 critical temperature is θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482. At utilisation μ₀ = 0.5, θ_cr ≈ 585°C; at μ₀ = 0.7 it drops to about 526°C, and at μ₀ = 0.3 it rises to about 664°C. Higher utilisation means a lower allowable steel temperature and thicker fire protection. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：結構計算書列出主要梁柱在火災荷載組合下的使用率與臨界溫度，與防火被覆廠商的厚度表一致；長跨樓板與關鍵柱另做結構火災分析，並在施工時以測厚儀抽查被覆厚度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The structural calculations list utilisation and critical temperature for principal beams and columns under the fire load combination, consistent with the fireproofing manufacturer's thickness tables; long-span floors and key columns receive structural fire analysis, and coating thickness is sampled with a gauge during construction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"EN 1993-1-2 臨界溫度 θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482。使用率 μ₀ = 0.5 時 θ_cr ≈ 585°C；μ₀ = 0.7 時降為約 526°C；μ₀ = 0.3 時升為約 664°C。使用率越高，允許的鋼材溫度越低，防火被覆要越厚。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The EN 1993-1-2 critical temperature is θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482. At utilisation μ₀ = 0.5, θ_cr ≈ 585°C; at μ₀ = 0.7 it drops to about 526°C, and at μ₀ = 0.3 it rises to about 664°C. Higher utilisation means a lower allowable steel temperature and thicker fire protection. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「區劃失效時的結構防火」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Structural fire safety when compartments fail\", which statement holds?","options":["防火區劃只是延緩火勢，真正滅火只能靠消防隊，所以區劃不必太嚴格。","EN 1993-1-2 臨界溫度 θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482。","防火門只要是防火材料做的，開著也能擋火。"],"optionsEn":["Compartments only delay a fire and only firefighters extinguish it, so compartmentation need not be rigorous.","The EN 1993-1-2 critical temperature is θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482.","A fire door made of fire-resisting material still stops fire when left open."],"answer":1,"explanation":"EN 1993-1-2 臨界溫度 θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The EN 1993-1-2 critical temperature is θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b091-v13-35","title":"區劃失效時的結構防火：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Structural fire safety when compartments fail: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼構臨界溫度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Steel critical temperature” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"結構計算書列出主要梁柱在火災荷載組合下的使用率與臨界溫度，與防火被覆廠商的厚度表一致；長跨樓板與關鍵柱另做結構火災分析，並在施工時以測厚儀抽查被覆厚度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The structural calculations list utilisation and critical temperature for principal beams and columns under the fire load combination, consistent with the fireproofing manufacturer's thickness tables; long-span floors and key columns receive structural fire analysis, and coating thickness is sampled with a gauge during construction. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：結構與消防設計應共同決定設計火災情境（單一區劃或多層火災）並寫入設計基準；被覆修補列入機電施工的退場檢查，使用期間的荷載增加須回饋到臨界溫度檢核。","observationEn":"Site practice: Structural and fire engineers should jointly set the design fire scenarios, single-compartment or multi-floor, in the design basis; fireproofing repair is part of services contractors' exit inspection, and added loads in service must feed back into critical-temperature checks.","failure":"注意干擾：若防火被覆依一般使用率設計，而某些構件因設計變更或增加荷載使用率提高，臨界溫度下降，同樣厚度的被覆在火災中提早失效；機電施工刮除或撞落被覆而未修補，也會形成局部弱點。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If fireproofing is sized for typical utilisation while design changes or added loads raise utilisation in some members, their critical temperature falls and the same coating fails early in a fire; fireproofing scraped or knocked off by services work and not repaired creates local weak points. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"結構計算書列出主要梁柱在火災荷載組合下的使用率與臨界溫度，與防火被覆廠商的厚度表一致；長跨樓板與關鍵柱另做結構火災分析，並在施工時以測厚儀抽查被覆厚度。","textEn":"The structural calculations list utilisation and critical temperature for principal beams and columns under the fire load combination, consistent with the fireproofing manufacturer's thickness tables; long-span floors and key columns receive structural fire analysis, and coating thickness is sampled with a gauge during construction.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"結構與消防設計應共同決定設計火災情境（單一區劃或多層火災）並寫入設計基準；被覆修補列入機電施工的退場檢查，使用期間的荷載增加須回饋到臨界溫度檢核。","textEn":"Structural and fire engineers should jointly set the design fire scenarios, single-compartment or multi-floor, in the design basis; fireproofing repair is part of services contractors' exit inspection, and added loads in service must feed back into critical-temperature checks.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「區劃失效時的結構防火」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Structural fire safety when compartments fail\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","管線穿過防火牆後，用任何填縫材料補起來就可以。","結構計算書列出主要梁柱在火災荷載組合下的使用率與臨界溫度，與防火被覆廠商的厚度表一致；長跨樓板與關鍵柱另做結構火災分析，並在施工時以測厚儀抽查被覆厚度。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","After pipes pass through a fire wall, any filler material can seal the gap.","The structural calculations list utilisation and critical temperature for principal beams and columns under the fire load combination, consistent with the fireproofing manufacturer's thickness tables."],"answer":2,"explanation":"結構計算書列出主要梁柱在火災荷載組合下的使用率與臨界溫度，與防火被覆廠商的厚度表一致；長跨樓板與關鍵柱另做結構火災分析，並在施工時以測厚儀抽查被覆厚度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The structural calculations list utilisation and critical temperature for principal beams and columns under the fire load combination, consistent with the fireproofing manufacturer's thickness tables; long-span floors and key columns receive structural fire analysis, and coating thickness is sampled with a gauge during construction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b091-v13-36","title":"區劃失效時的結構防火：失效診斷","titleEn":"Structural fire safety when compartments fail: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼構臨界溫度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Steel critical temperature” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若防火被覆依一般使用率設計，而某些構件因設計變更或增加荷載使用率提高，臨界溫度下降，同樣厚度的被覆在火災中提早失效；機電施工刮除或撞落被覆而未修補，也會形成局部弱點。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If fireproofing is sized for typical utilisation while design changes or added loads raise utilisation in some members, their critical temperature falls and the same coating fails early in a fire; fireproofing scraped or knocked off by services work and not repaired creates local weak points. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：結構工程師要知道構件在多高的溫度會失去承載力，並與防火被覆的設計溫度一致。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Structural engineers must know the temperature at which members lose capacity and align it with the fireproofing design temperature.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼構只要有防火被覆，區劃失效也不會影響結構安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Steelwork with fireproofing is safe even if compartmentation fails.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若防火被覆依一般使用率設計，而某些構件因設計變更或增加荷載使用率提高，臨界溫度下降，同樣厚度的被覆在火災中提早失效；機電施工刮除或撞落被覆而未修補，也會形成局部弱點。","textEn":"If fireproofing is sized for typical utilisation while design changes or added loads raise utilisation in some members, their critical temperature falls and the same coating fails early in a fire; fireproofing scraped or knocked off by services work and not repaired creates local weak points.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「區劃失效時的結構防火」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Structural fire safety when compartments fail\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若防火被覆依一般使用率設計，而某些構件因設計變更或增加荷載使用率提高，臨界溫度下降，同樣厚度的被覆在火災中提早失效。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","老舊建築只要當年合法取得使用執照，就不需要再檢討防火區劃。"],"optionsEn":["If fireproofing is sized for typical utilisation while design changes or added loads raise utilisation in some members, their critical temperature falls and the same coating fails early in a fire.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","An old building that was lawfully approved when built needs no further review of its compartmentation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若防火被覆依一般使用率設計，而某些構件因設計變更或增加荷載使用率提高，臨界溫度下降，同樣厚度的被覆在火災中提早失效；機電施工刮除或撞落被覆而未修補，也會形成局部弱點。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If fireproofing is sized for typical utilisation while design changes or added loads raise utilisation in some members, their critical temperature falls and the same coating fails early in a fire; fireproofing scraped or knocked off by services work and not repaired creates local weak points. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b091-v13-37","title":"使用管理、避難時間與交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Management in use, escape time and handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「區劃管理與公共安全申報」如何影響高層建築消防分區設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Compartment management and safety reporting” governs force, deformation or durability in “Fire compartmentation in high-rise buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"區劃在使用期間最容易被破壞：防火門被撐開、走廊堆放雜物、隔間任意變更、管道間被打開。2021 年 10 月高雄 13 層的城中城大樓火災造成 46 人死亡、41 人受傷，火從一樓起火，因低樓層挑高與玻璃立面迅速竄升，濃煙充滿上方樓層，雜物又助長火勢並阻礙救援，多數死者因吸入濃煙而亡。這類老舊大樓顯示，區劃不只是設計問題，而是管理、檢查與住戶教育的長期責任。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「區劃管理與公共安全申報」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compartments are most easily defeated in use: fire doors propped open, corridors cluttered, partitions altered at will and shafts opened. The October 2021 fire at Kaohsiung's 13-storey Cheng Chung Cheng Building killed 46 people and injured 41; starting on the ground floor, it rose quickly through high-ceilinged lower floors with a glass frontage and filled the floors above with smoke, while clutter fed the fire and blocked rescue, and most victims died of smoke inhalation. Such ageing buildings show that compartmentation is not only a design issue but a long-term responsibility of management, inspection and occupant education. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Compartment management and safety reporting” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以可用避難時間與所需避難時間比較：RSET = 偵測 60 s + 反應準備 300 s（夜間睡眠）+ 移動 180 s = 540 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Compare available and required safe egress time: RSET = detection 60 s + pre-movement 300 s (asleep at night) + travel 180 s = 540 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「老舊建築只要當年合法取得使用執照，就不需要再檢討防火區劃。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An old building that was lawfully approved when built needs no further review of its compartmentation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「區劃管理與公共安全申報」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Compartment management and safety reporting”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-37-k1","title":"使用管理、避難時間與交接","titleEn":"Management in use, escape time and handover","text":"區劃在使用期間最容易被破壞：防火門被撐開、走廊堆放雜物、隔間任意變更、管道間被打開。2021 年 10 月高雄 13 層的城中城大樓火災造成 46 人死亡、41 人受傷，火從一樓起火，因低樓層挑高與玻璃立面迅速竄升，濃煙充滿上方樓層，雜物又助長火勢並阻礙救援，多數死者因吸入濃煙而亡。","textEn":"Compartments are most easily defeated in use: fire doors propped open, corridors cluttered, partitions altered at will and shafts opened. The October 2021 fire at Kaohsiung's 13-storey Cheng Chung Cheng Building killed 46 people and injured 41; starting on the ground floor, it rose quickly through high-ceilinged lower floors with a glass frontage and filled the floors above with smoke, while clutter fed the fire and blocked rescue, and most victims died of smoke inhalation.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：老舊建築只要當年合法取得使用執照，就不需要再檢討防火區劃。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An old building that was lawfully approved when built needs no further review of its compartmentation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「使用管理、避難時間與交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Management in use, escape time and handover\" is correct?","options":["老舊建築只要當年合法取得使用執照，就不需要再檢討防火區劃。","區劃在使用期間最容易被破壞：防火門被撐開、走廊堆放雜物、隔間任意變更、管道間被打開。","只要設了灑水系統，防火區劃就可有可無。"],"optionsEn":["An old building that was lawfully approved when built needs no further review of its compartmentation.","Compartments are most easily defeated in use: fire doors propped open, corridors cluttered, partitions altered at will and shafts opened.","With sprinklers installed, compartmentation is optional."],"answer":1,"explanation":"區劃在使用期間最容易被破壞：防火門被撐開、走廊堆放雜物、隔間任意變更、管道間被打開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compartments are most easily defeated in use: fire doors propped open, corridors cluttered, partitions altered at will and shafts opened. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b091-v13-38","title":"使用管理、避難時間與交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Management in use, escape time and handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「區劃管理與公共安全申報」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Compartment management and safety reporting” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以可用避難時間與所需避難時間比較：RSET = 偵測 60 s + 反應準備 300 s（夜間睡眠）+ 移動 180 s = 540 s。若區劃失效、快速成長火災使走廊約 300 s 就不可維生，ASET − RSET = 300 − 540 = −240 s；區劃與防火門完整而把走廊維生時間延長到 900 s 以上，才有 360 s 的餘裕。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Compare available and required safe egress time: RSET = detection 60 s + pre-movement 300 s (asleep at night) + travel 180 s = 540 s. If compartments fail and a fast fire makes the corridor untenable at about 300 s, ASET − RSET = 300 − 540 = −240 s; only intact compartments and doors that extend corridor tenability beyond 900 s leave a margin of 360 s. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：管理單位依建築物公共安全檢查與消防安全設備檢修申報制度定期檢查防火門、區劃牆、貫穿填塞、樓梯淨空與灑水系統，檢查結果與防火區劃圖比對；改裝前由建築師或專業技師確認不破壞區劃。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Managers inspect fire doors, compartment walls, penetration seals, stair clearance and sprinklers periodically under building public-safety inspection and fire-protection equipment reporting schemes, comparing results with the compartmentation plan; before alterations an architect or professional engineer confirms that compartments are not breached.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以可用避難時間與所需避難時間比較：RSET = 偵測 60 s + 反應準備 300 s（夜間睡眠）+ 移動 180 s = 540 s。若區劃失效、快速成長火災使走廊約 300 s 就不可維生，ASET − RSET = 300 − 540 = −240 s；區劃與防火門完整而把走廊維生時間延長到 900 s 以上，才有 360 s 的餘裕。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Compare available and required safe egress time: RSET = detection 60 s + pre-movement 300 s (asleep at night) + travel 180 s = 540 s. If compartments fail and a fast fire makes the corridor untenable at about 300 s, ASET − RSET = 300 − 540 = −240 s; only intact compartments and doors that extend corridor tenability beyond 900 s leave a margin of 360 s. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「使用管理、避難時間與交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Management in use, escape time and handover\", which statement holds?","options":["標示一小時防火時效的牆，在任何火災中都一定能撐一小時。","樓板本身有防火時效，就代表上下樓層已經完全區劃。","以可用避難時間與所需避難時間比較：RSET = 偵測 60 s + 反應準備 300 s（夜間睡眠）+ 移動 180 s = 540 s。"],"optionsEn":["A wall rated for one hour will always last one hour in any fire.","If the floor slab is fire-rated, the floors above and below are fully compartmented.","Compare available and required safe egress time: RSET = detection 60 s + pre-movement 300 s (asleep at night) + travel 180 s = 540 s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以可用避難時間與所需避難時間比較：RSET = 偵測 60 s + 反應準備 300 s（夜間睡眠）+ 移動 180 s = 540 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Compare available and required safe egress time: RSET = detection 60 s + pre-movement 300 s (asleep at night) + travel 180 s = 540 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b091-v13-39","title":"使用管理、避難時間與交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Management in use, escape time and handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「區劃管理與公共安全申報」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Compartment management and safety reporting” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"管理單位依建築物公共安全檢查與消防安全設備檢修申報制度定期檢查防火門、區劃牆、貫穿填塞、樓梯淨空與灑水系統，檢查結果與防火區劃圖比對；改裝前由建築師或專業技師確認不破壞區劃。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Managers inspect fire doors, compartment walls, penetration seals, stair clearance and sprinklers periodically under building public-safety inspection and fire-protection equipment reporting schemes, comparing results with the compartmentation plan; before alterations an architect or professional engineer confirms that compartments are not breached. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件應包含防火區劃圖、防火構造試驗報告清單、防火門與貫穿部登錄、加壓與灑水系統驗收紀錄、檢查週期與改裝許可流程；管理單位應定期辦理住戶防火教育，並把防火門常閉列入規約。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover should include the compartmentation plan, a list of fire-test reports, registers of fire doors and penetrations, acceptance records for pressurisation and sprinklers, inspection intervals and the alteration permit procedure; managers should run regular occupant fire education and write ‘fire doors kept closed’ into house rules.","failure":"注意干擾：若交接文件沒有防火區劃圖與貫穿部登錄，後續管理者不知道哪些牆是區劃牆，裝修時任意打通或開孔；長期堆放雜物與撐開防火門，讓設計上可行的避難時間在真實火災中變成負值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without a compartmentation plan and penetration register at handover, later managers cannot tell which walls are compartment walls and break through or cut them during renovation; years of clutter and propped-open fire doors turn an escape margin that worked in design into a negative one in a real fire. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"管理單位依建築物公共安全檢查與消防安全設備檢修申報制度定期檢查防火門、區劃牆、貫穿填塞、樓梯淨空與灑水系統，檢查結果與防火區劃圖比對；改裝前由建築師或專業技師確認不破壞區劃。","textEn":"Managers inspect fire doors, compartment walls, penetration seals, stair clearance and sprinklers periodically under building public-safety inspection and fire-protection equipment reporting schemes, comparing results with the compartmentation plan; before alterations an architect or professional engineer confirms that compartments are not breached.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件應包含防火區劃圖、防火構造試驗報告清單、防火門與貫穿部登錄、加壓與灑水系統驗收紀錄、檢查週期與改裝許可流程；管理單位應定期辦理住戶防火教育，並把防火門常閉列入規約。","textEn":"Handover should include the compartmentation plan, a list of fire-test reports, registers of fire doors and penetrations, acceptance records for pressurisation and sprinklers, inspection intervals and the alteration permit procedure; managers should run regular occupant fire education and write ‘fire doors kept closed’ into house rules.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「使用管理、避難時間與交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Management in use, escape time and handover\"?","options":["管理單位依建築物公共安全檢查與消防安全設備檢修申報制度定期檢查防火門、區劃牆、貫穿填塞、樓梯淨空與灑水系統，檢查結果與防火區劃圖比對。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要材料本身不燃，組成的牆或門就自動具有防火時效。"],"optionsEn":["Managers inspect fire doors, compartment walls, penetration seals, stair clearance and sprinklers periodically under building public-safety inspection and fire-protection equipment reporting schemes, comparing results with the compartmentation plan.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","If the materials are non-combustible, the wall or door they form automatically has a fire rating."],"answer":0,"explanation":"管理單位依建築物公共安全檢查與消防安全設備檢修申報制度定期檢查防火門、區劃牆、貫穿填塞、樓梯淨空與灑水系統，檢查結果與防火區劃圖比對；改裝前由建築師或專業技師確認不破壞區劃。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Managers inspect fire doors, compartment walls, penetration seals, stair clearance and sprinklers periodically under building public-safety inspection and fire-protection equipment reporting schemes, comparing results with the compartmentation plan; before alterations an architect or professional engineer confirms that compartments are not breached. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b091-v13-40","title":"使用管理、避難時間與交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Management in use, escape time and handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"prerequisiteIds":["b091-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「區劃管理與公共安全申報」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Compartment management and safety reporting” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若交接文件沒有防火區劃圖與貫穿部登錄，後續管理者不知道哪些牆是區劃牆，裝修時任意打通或開孔；長期堆放雜物與撐開防火門，讓設計上可行的避難時間在真實火災中變成負值。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without a compartmentation plan and penetration register at handover, later managers cannot tell which walls are compartment walls and break through or cut them during renovation; years of clutter and propped-open fire doors turn an escape margin that worked in design into a negative one in a real fire. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這類老舊大樓顯示，區劃不只是設計問題，而是管理、檢查與住戶教育的長期責任。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Such ageing buildings show that compartmentation is not only a design issue but a long-term responsibility of management, inspection and occupant education.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「老舊建築只要當年合法取得使用執照，就不需要再檢討防火區劃。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An old building that was lawfully approved when built needs no further review of its compartmentation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b091-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若交接文件沒有防火區劃圖與貫穿部登錄，後續管理者不知道哪些牆是區劃牆，裝修時任意打通或開孔；長期堆放雜物與撐開防火門，讓設計上可行的避難時間在真實火災中變成負值。","textEn":"Without a compartmentation plan and penetration register at handover, later managers cannot tell which walls are compartment walls and break through or cut them during renovation; years of clutter and propped-open fire doors turn an escape margin that worked in design into a negative one in a real fire.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]},{"id":"b091-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「使用管理、避難時間與交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Management in use, escape time and handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若交接文件沒有防火區劃圖與貫穿部登錄，後續管理者不知道哪些牆是區劃牆，裝修時任意打通或開孔。","只要設了灑水系統，防火區劃就可有可無。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Without a compartmentation plan and penetration register at handover, later managers cannot tell which walls are compartment walls and break through or cut them during renovation.","With sprinklers installed, compartmentation is optional."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若交接文件沒有防火區劃圖與貫穿部登錄，後續管理者不知道哪些牆是區劃牆，裝修時任意打通或開孔；長期堆放雜物與撐開防火門，讓設計上可行的避難時間在真實火災中變成負值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without a compartmentation plan and penetration register at handover, later managers cannot tell which walls are compartment walls and break through or cut them during renovation; years of clutter and propped-open fire doors turn an escape margin that worked in design into a negative one in a real fire. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-grenfell-phase-1","v13s-nist-wtc7-faq","v13s-wiki-kaohsiung-fire","v13s-wiki-one-meridian-plaza","v13s-wiki-grenfell-fire"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
